' =============================================================================
' PACMAN CLONE - A Beginner's Guide to Game Programming
' =============================================================================
'
' Welcome! This is a complete PacMan game written in DBasic.
'
' HOW A GAME WORKS (the big picture):
'   A game is like a flipbook. The computer draws a picture (a "frame"),
'   shows it to you, then draws the next picture with things moved slightly.
'   It does this 60 times per second, so it looks like smooth motion.
'
'   Every frame, the game does 3 things:
'     1. CHECK INPUT  - What buttons is the player pressing?
'     2. UPDATE       - Move PacMan, move ghosts, check collisions
'     3. DRAW         - Paint everything on screen
'
' HOW THE MAZE WORKS:
'   The maze is a grid of 28 columns x 31 rows. Each cell in the grid
'   is one of: wall, dot, power pellet, empty space, or ghost house door.
'   Think of it like graph paper where each square has a type.
'
' HOW MOVEMENT WORKS:
'   Characters don't just jump from tile to tile. They slide smoothly
'   between tiles, moving 2 pixels at a time. A tile is 16 pixels wide,
'   so it takes 8 "steps" to cross one tile. Characters can only change
'   direction when they're exactly at the center of a tile.
'
' HOW SPEED WORKS:
'   Different characters move at different speeds (PacMan at 80%,
'   ghosts at 75%, etc). We use an "accumulator" trick: each frame,
'   we add the speed percentage to a counter. When the counter hits 100,
'   the character takes one step. So at 80% speed, the character moves
'   on 4 out of every 5 frames. This keeps speed consistent on any computer.
'
' GAME MODES:
'   - 1 Player:         Classic solo PacMan. Arrow keys or WASD.
'   - 2P Alternating:   Players take turns. When one dies, the other plays.
'                        Both use arrow keys. Separate scores and lives.
'   - 2P Co-op:         Both players on screen at once! P1=WASD, P2=Arrows.
'                        Shared maze, separate scores. Ghosts chase nearest.
'
' HIGH SCORES:
'   Top 5 scores saved to "pacman_scores.txt". If you qualify, enter your
'   3-letter initials using Up/Down to pick letters and Left/Right to move.
'
' Controls: Arrow keys or WASD to move, Enter to select menu items
' =============================================================================

' ======================== IMPORTS ========================
' These bring in code libraries that other people wrote, so we don't
' have to build everything from scratch. It's like using LEGO pieces
' someone else designed.

' Ebitengine is a "game engine" - it handles the window, drawing, and
' running our game loop 60 times per second.
IMPORT "github.com/hajimehoshi/ebiten/v2" AS ebiten

' The "vector" package lets us draw shapes like circles and rectangles.
IMPORT "github.com/hajimehoshi/ebiten/v2/vector" AS vector

' This gives us a simple way to draw text on screen (for score, messages).
IMPORT "github.com/hajimehoshi/ebiten/v2/ebitenutil" AS ebitenutil

' inpututil gives us IsKeyJustPressed for single-press detection.
IMPORT "github.com/hajimehoshi/ebiten/v2/inpututil" AS inpututil

' Colors! We need this to say things like "draw this circle in yellow."
IMPORT "image/color" AS color

' For printing error messages if something goes wrong.
IMPORT "fmt" AS fmt

' Audio support - lets us play sound effects!
IMPORT "github.com/hajimehoshi/ebiten/v2/audio" AS audio

' String reader - used to feed generated audio data to the audio player.
IMPORT "strings" AS strings

' strconv for parsing integers from strings.
IMPORT "strconv" AS strconv


' Global audio context - Ebitengine only allows ONE audio context per program.
' We create it once in Main() and share it with the game.
DIM GAudioCtx AS POINTER TO audio.Context

' ======================== CONSTANTS ========================
' Constants are values that never change while the game is running.
' We give them names so the code is easier to read.
' For example, writing "TILE" is clearer than writing "16" everywhere.

' Each square in our maze grid is 16x16 pixels on screen.
CONST TILE AS INTEGER = 16

' The maze is 28 tiles wide and 31 tiles tall (just like the real PacMan!).
CONST MW AS INTEGER = 28
CONST MH AS INTEGER = 31

' Screen size in pixels. Width = 28 tiles * 16 pixels = 448 pixels.
' Height = 31 tiles * 16 + room for score display = 560 pixels.
CONST SCRW AS INTEGER = 448
CONST SCRH AS INTEGER = 560

' The score display takes up 32 pixels at the top of the screen.
' Everything in the maze is shifted down by this amount.
CONST HUD_TOP AS INTEGER = 32

' Each "step" of movement is 2 pixels. Since tiles are 16 pixels wide,
' it takes 8 steps to cross one tile (16 / 2 = 8).
CONST PX_STEP AS INTEGER = 2

' --- CELL TYPES ---
' Each square in the maze grid is one of these types.
' We use numbers as codes so the computer can quickly check what's there.
CONST C_EMPTY AS INTEGER = 0
CONST C_WALL AS INTEGER = 1
CONST C_DOT AS INTEGER = 2
CONST C_POWER AS INTEGER = 3
CONST C_DOOR AS INTEGER = 4

' --- DIRECTIONS ---
' We represent directions as numbers. When PacMan is heading left,
' his direction is set to 3 (D_LEFT).
CONST D_NONE AS INTEGER = 0
CONST D_UP AS INTEGER = 1
CONST D_DOWN AS INTEGER = 2
CONST D_LEFT AS INTEGER = 3
CONST D_RIGHT AS INTEGER = 4

' --- GHOST MODES ---
' Ghosts change behavior depending on their "mode." Think of modes
' like moods - sometimes they're chasing you, sometimes they're scared.
'
' SCATTER: Ghosts retreat to their assigned corner of the maze.
' CHASE:   Ghosts actively hunt PacMan (each ghost has a unique strategy).
' FRIGHT:  Ghosts are scared (after PacMan eats a power pellet) and run away.
' EATEN:   Ghost was eaten by PacMan - only the eyes remain, rushing back to jail.
' HOUSE:   Ghost is waiting inside the "ghost house" (jail) to be released.
' ENTER:   Ghost eyes are moving down into the ghost house after being eaten.
' LEAVE:   Ghost is floating up out of the ghost house to rejoin the game.
CONST M_SCATTER AS INTEGER = 0
CONST M_CHASE AS INTEGER = 1
CONST M_FRIGHT AS INTEGER = 2
CONST M_EATEN AS INTEGER = 3
CONST M_HOUSE AS INTEGER = 4
CONST M_ENTER AS INTEGER = 5
CONST M_LEAVE AS INTEGER = 6

' --- GAME STATES ---
' The game itself has states too. It can be showing "READY!", actively
' playing, showing PacMan's death animation, showing "GAME OVER",
' celebrating a cleared level, on the title screen, or entering initials.
CONST S_READY AS INTEGER = 0
CONST S_PLAY AS INTEGER = 1
CONST S_DYING AS INTEGER = 2
CONST S_OVER AS INTEGER = 3
CONST S_WON AS INTEGER = 4
CONST S_INTRO AS INTEGER = 5
CONST S_HISCORE AS INTEGER = 6

' --- GAME MODES ---
' Single player, 2-player alternating (take turns), 2-player co-op (simultaneous).
CONST GM_SINGLE AS INTEGER = 0
CONST GM_ALTER AS INTEGER = 1
CONST GM_COOP AS INTEGER = 2

' --- SPEED PERCENTAGES ---
' These control how fast everything moves. 100 = full speed (move every frame).
' 80 = move on 4 out of every 5 frames. 50 = move on every other frame.
' These match the speeds from the original PacMan arcade game!
'
' The speed system works like a piggy bank:
'   - Each frame, you put in coins equal to your speed (e.g., 80 coins)
'   - When you have 100 coins or more, you get to move and spend 100 coins
'   - At 80% speed: frame 1 (80), frame 2 (160->move->60), frame 3 (140->move->40)...
'   - This means you move slightly less often than full speed
CONST SPD_PAC AS INTEGER = 80
CONST SPD_PAC_DOT AS INTEGER = 71
CONST SPD_GHOST AS INTEGER = 75
CONST SPD_FRIGHT_PAC AS INTEGER = 90
CONST SPD_FRIGHT_GHOST AS INTEGER = 50
CONST SPD_TUNNEL AS INTEGER = 40
CONST SPD_EYES AS INTEGER = 150
CONST SPD_HOUSE AS INTEGER = 30

' --- TIMERS ---
' These are measured in "ticks" (frames). At 60 frames per second:
'   120 ticks = 2 seconds, 360 ticks = 6 seconds, etc.
CONST T_READY AS INTEGER = 120
CONST T_DYING AS INTEGER = 60
CONST T_FRIGHT AS INTEGER = 360
CONST T_FLASH AS INTEGER = 120

' --- POSITIONS ---
' Where PacMan and the ghost house are located on the grid.
CONST PAC_SX AS INTEGER = 14
CONST PAC_SY AS INTEGER = 23
CONST TUNNEL_Y AS INTEGER = 14

' The ghost house ("jail") has three key locations:
' - The DOOR is where ghosts enter/exit (the pink line in the maze)
' - The CENTER is where ghosts wait inside
' - The EXIT is just above the door where ghosts emerge
CONST HOUSE_DOOR_X AS INTEGER = 14
CONST HOUSE_DOOR_Y AS INTEGER = 12
CONST HOUSE_CENTER_X AS INTEGER = 14
CONST HOUSE_CENTER_Y AS INTEGER = 14
CONST HOUSE_EXIT_X AS INTEGER = 14
CONST HOUSE_EXIT_Y AS INTEGER = 11

' --- GHOST RELEASE THRESHOLDS ---
' Ghosts start inside the house and are released one by one as PacMan
' eats dots. Pinky comes out almost immediately, Inky after 30 dots,
' and Clyde (the slowpoke) after 60 dots.
CONST REL_PINKY AS INTEGER = 1
CONST REL_INKY AS INTEGER = 30
CONST REL_CLYDE AS INTEGER = 60

' --- HIGH SCORE CONSTANTS ---
' We keep 5 high scores. The file name is hardcoded.
CONST MAX_HISCORES AS INTEGER = 5
CONST HISCORE_FILE AS STRING = "pacman_scores.txt"

' ======================== TYPES (Data Structures) ========================
' A TYPE is like a form or template. It groups related information together.
' Think of it like a character sheet in a board game - it holds all the
' stats for one character in one place.

' --- GHOST ---
' Each ghost has its own position, direction, behavior mode, etc.
TYPE Ghost
    DIM X AS INTEGER            ' Horizontal pixel position (not tile, but exact pixel)
    DIM Y AS INTEGER            ' Vertical pixel position
    DIM Dir AS INTEGER          ' Which way the ghost is currently moving (D_UP, D_LEFT, etc.)
    DIM GType AS INTEGER        ' Which ghost this is: 0=Blinky, 1=Pinky, 2=Inky, 3=Clyde
    DIM Mode AS INTEGER         ' Current behavior mode (M_CHASE, M_FRIGHT, M_EATEN, etc.)
    DIM FTimer AS INTEGER       ' Countdown timer for how long the ghost stays frightened
    DIM ScatX AS INTEGER        ' X tile of this ghost's "scatter corner" (where it retreats to)
    DIM ScatY AS INTEGER        ' Y tile of this ghost's "scatter corner"
    DIM MoveAcc AS INTEGER      ' Speed accumulator (the "piggy bank" described above)
    DIM HouseTimer AS INTEGER   ' Countdown for how long to wait inside the house before leaving
END TYPE

' --- PLAYER ---
' Each player (1 or 2) has their own PacMan with position, score, lives, etc.
' In co-op, both players are on screen at once. In alternating, they take turns.
' The Clr field is 0 for yellow (P1) and 1 for green (P2).
TYPE Player
    DIM PX AS INTEGER           ' PacMan's X pixel position
    DIM PY AS INTEGER           ' PacMan's Y pixel position
    DIM PDir AS INTEGER         ' PacMan's current movement direction
    DIM PNext AS INTEGER        ' The direction the player WANTS PacMan to go next
    DIM PMoveAcc AS INTEGER     ' PacMan's speed accumulator
    DIM Mouth AS BOOLEAN        ' Is PacMan's mouth open? (toggles for animation)
    DIM MouthT AS INTEGER       ' Timer for mouth open/close animation
    DIM Score AS INTEGER        ' Player's score (10 per dot, 50 per power pellet, 200+ per ghost)
    DIM Lives AS INTEGER        ' How many lives PacMan has left
    DIM IFrames AS INTEGER      ' Invincibility frames (not currently used, reserved)
    DIM Alive AS BOOLEAN        ' Is this player currently alive? (for co-op)
    DIM Clr AS INTEGER          ' 0=yellow (P1), 1=green (P2)
END TYPE

' --- HISCORE ENTRY ---
' One entry in the high score table. Has 3-letter initials and a score.
TYPE HiEntry
    DIM Initials AS STRING      ' 3 letters, e.g. "ACE"
    DIM Pts AS INTEGER          ' The score
END TYPE

' --- GAME ---
' This holds EVERYTHING about the current game: the maze, players,
' all 4 ghosts, game mode, high scores, etc.
' It's like the "game board" that contains the entire state of the game.
TYPE Game
    DIM Maze AS []INTEGER       ' The maze grid stored as a flat list (28*31 = 868 cells)
    DIM Gh AS []Ghost           ' Array of 4 ghosts (Blinky, Pinky, Inky, Clyde)
    DIM Level AS INTEGER        ' Current level number
    DIM Eaten AS INTEGER        ' How many dots have been eaten this level
    DIM Total AS INTEGER        ' Total number of dots in the maze (eat them all to win!)
    DIM State AS INTEGER        ' Current game state (S_READY, S_PLAY, S_DYING, etc.)
    DIM STimer AS INTEGER       ' General-purpose state timer (counts down for animations)
    DIM GMode AS INTEGER        ' The current global ghost mode (scatter or chase)
    DIM MTimer AS INTEGER       ' Timer for the scatter/chase cycle
    DIM MPhase AS INTEGER       ' Which phase of the scatter/chase cycle we're in
    DIM GScore AS INTEGER       ' Points for eating the next ghost (doubles: 200, 400, 800, 1600)
    DIM Frame AS INTEGER        ' Total frames elapsed (used for blinking animations)
    DIM EPause AS INTEGER       ' Brief pause when PacMan eats a dot (makes eating feel crunchy)
    DIM WallImg AS POINTER TO ebiten.Image  ' Pre-drawn image of all walls (performance optimization)

    ' --- MULTIPLAYER FIELDS ---
    DIM Pl AS []Player          ' Array of players (1 or 2 depending on mode)
    DIM NumPl AS INTEGER        ' Number of players (1 or 2)
    DIM CurPl AS INTEGER        ' Index of current player in alternating mode (0 or 1)
    DIM GmMode AS INTEGER       ' Game mode: GM_SINGLE, GM_ALTER, GM_COOP

    ' --- MENU / INTRO FIELDS ---
    DIM MenuSel AS INTEGER      ' Currently highlighted menu option (0, 1, or 2)

    ' --- HIGH SCORE FIELDS ---
    DIM HiScores AS []HiEntry   ' Top 5 high scores
    DIM HiName AS []INTEGER     ' 3 letter codes (0-25 = A-Z) being entered
    DIM HiCursor AS INTEGER     ' Which letter position the cursor is on (0, 1, or 2)
    DIM HiSlot AS INTEGER       ' Which slot in the table this score goes into
    DIM HiPlIdx AS INTEGER      ' Which player is entering their score (0 or 1)
    DIM HiDone0 AS BOOLEAN      ' Has P1 finished entering their initials?
    DIM HiDone1 AS BOOLEAN      ' Has P2 finished entering their initials?

    ' --- ALTERNATING MODE FIELDS ---
    DIM AltMaze0 AS []INTEGER   ' Saved maze state for player 0
    DIM AltMaze1 AS []INTEGER   ' Saved maze state for player 1
    DIM AltEaten0 AS INTEGER    ' Saved eaten count for player 0
    DIM AltEaten1 AS INTEGER    ' Saved eaten count for player 1
    DIM AltDying AS INTEGER     ' Which player is dying in alternating mode

    ' --- SOUND PLAYERS ---
    DIM SndWaka AS POINTER TO audio.Player   ' "waka" sound when eating a dot
    DIM SndPower AS POINTER TO audio.Player  ' sound when eating a power pellet
    DIM SndEatGh AS POINTER TO audio.Player  ' sound when eating a ghost
    DIM SndDie AS POINTER TO audio.Player    ' sound when PacMan dies
    DIM SndReady AS POINTER TO audio.Player  ' jingle at start of round
    DIM SndWon AS POINTER TO audio.Player    ' sound when level is cleared
    DIM SndMenu AS POINTER TO audio.Player   ' blip for menu selection
END TYPE

' ======================== MAZE LAYOUT ========================
' The maze is defined as text art! Each character represents one tile:
'   # = Wall (blue blocks you can't walk through)
'   . = Dot (small pellet worth 10 points)
'   o = Power Pellet (big blinking pellet that lets you eat ghosts!)
'   - = Ghost House Door (ghosts can pass through, PacMan cannot)
'   (space) = Empty walkable space
'
' This is the classic PacMan maze layout - 28 characters wide, 31 rows tall.
' The ghost house is in the middle (rows 12-16), and the tunnel that wraps
' around from left to right is on row 14.

FUNCTION GetMazeLayout() AS []STRING
    DIM m AS []STRING
    m = APPEND(m, "############################")
    m = APPEND(m, "#............##............#")
    m = APPEND(m, "#.####.#####.##.#####.####.#")
    m = APPEND(m, "#o####.#####.##.#####.####o#")
    m = APPEND(m, "#.####.#####.##.#####.####.#")
    m = APPEND(m, "#..........................#")
    m = APPEND(m, "#.####.##.########.##.####.#")
    m = APPEND(m, "#.####.##.########.##.####.#")
    m = APPEND(m, "#......##....##....##......#")
    m = APPEND(m, "######.#####.##.#####.######")
    m = APPEND(m, "     #.#####.##.#####.#     ")
    m = APPEND(m, "     #.##          ##.#     ")
    m = APPEND(m, "     #.## ###--### ##.#     ")
    m = APPEND(m, "######.## #      # ##.######")
    m = APPEND(m, "      .   #      #   .      ")
    m = APPEND(m, "######.## #      # ##.######")
    m = APPEND(m, "     #.## ######## ##.#     ")
    m = APPEND(m, "     #.##          ##.#     ")
    m = APPEND(m, "     #.## ######## ##.#     ")
    m = APPEND(m, "######.## ######## ##.######")
    m = APPEND(m, "#............##............#")
    m = APPEND(m, "#.####.#####.##.#####.####.#")
    m = APPEND(m, "#.####.#####.##.#####.####.#")
    m = APPEND(m, "#o..##.......  .......##..o#")
    m = APPEND(m, "###.##.##.########.##.##.###")
    m = APPEND(m, "###.##.##.########.##.##.###")
    m = APPEND(m, "#......##....##....##......#")
    m = APPEND(m, "#.##########.##.##########.#")
    m = APPEND(m, "#.##########.##.##########.#")
    m = APPEND(m, "#..........................#")
    m = APPEND(m, "############################")
    RETURN m
END FUNCTION

' ======================== HELPER FUNCTIONS ========================
' These are small utility functions used throughout the code.
' Think of them as tools in a toolbox.

' T2P: "Tile to Pixel" - converts a tile coordinate to a pixel position.
' It returns the CENTER of the tile, not the top-left corner.
' Example: tile 3 -> pixel 3*16 + 8 = 56 (the center of a 16px-wide tile)
FUNCTION T2P(t AS INTEGER) AS INTEGER
    RETURN t * TILE + TILE / 2
END FUNCTION

' P2T: "Pixel to Tile" - converts a pixel position back to a tile coordinate.
' Example: pixel 56 -> tile 56/16 = 3
FUNCTION P2T(p AS INTEGER) AS INTEGER
    IF p < 0 THEN RETURN -1
    RETURN p / TILE
END FUNCTION

' AtCenter: Checks if a pixel position is exactly at the center of a tile.
' Characters can only change direction when they're at a tile center.
' The center of any tile has coordinates where (x mod 16 == 8) and (y mod 16 == 8).
FUNCTION AtCenter(x AS INTEGER, y AS INTEGER) AS BOOLEAN
    RETURN (x MOD TILE = TILE / 2) AND (y MOD TILE = TILE / 2)
END FUNCTION

' Opposite: Returns the reverse of a direction (UP<->DOWN, LEFT<->RIGHT).
' Used when ghosts need to turn around.
FUNCTION Opposite(d AS INTEGER) AS INTEGER
    IF d = D_UP THEN RETURN D_DOWN
    IF d = D_DOWN THEN RETURN D_UP
    IF d = D_LEFT THEN RETURN D_RIGHT
    IF d = D_RIGHT THEN RETURN D_LEFT
    RETURN D_NONE
END FUNCTION

' DirDX and DirDY: Convert a direction into X and Y offsets.
' LEFT = -1 on X axis, RIGHT = +1 on X axis, UP = -1 on Y axis, etc.
' (In computer graphics, Y increases DOWNWARD, so "up" is negative Y.)
FUNCTION DirDX(d AS INTEGER) AS INTEGER
    IF d = D_LEFT THEN RETURN -1
    IF d = D_RIGHT THEN RETURN 1
    RETURN 0
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION DirDY(d AS INTEGER) AS INTEGER
    IF d = D_UP THEN RETURN -1
    IF d = D_DOWN THEN RETURN 1
    RETURN 0
END FUNCTION

' Cell: Looks up what type of cell is at a given tile position in the maze.
' If you ask about a tile outside the maze, it returns WALL (can't go there).
' Special case: the tunnel row (row 14) wraps around, so tiles off the
' left/right edge are treated as EMPTY on that row.
FUNCTION (g AS POINTER TO Game) Cell(tx AS INTEGER, ty AS INTEGER) AS INTEGER
    IF ty < 0 OR ty >= MH THEN RETURN C_WALL
    IF tx < 0 OR tx >= MW THEN
        IF ty = TUNNEL_Y THEN RETURN C_EMPTY
        RETURN C_WALL
    ENDIF
    RETURN g.Maze[ty * MW + tx]
END FUNCTION

' Passable: Can a character walk on this tile?
' Walls are never passable. The ghost house door is passable for ghosts
' but NOT for PacMan (the "pac" parameter tells us who's asking).
FUNCTION (g AS POINTER TO Game) Passable(tx AS INTEGER, ty AS INTEGER, pac AS BOOLEAN) AS BOOLEAN
    DIM c AS INTEGER = g.Cell(tx, ty)
    IF c = C_WALL THEN RETURN FALSE
    IF c = C_DOOR THEN
        IF pac THEN RETURN FALSE
    ENDIF
    RETURN TRUE
END FUNCTION

' CanGo: Can a character at tile (tx,ty) move in direction d?
' It checks the NEXT tile in that direction to see if it's passable.
FUNCTION (g AS POINTER TO Game) CanGo(tx AS INTEGER, ty AS INTEGER, d AS INTEGER, pac AS BOOLEAN) AS BOOLEAN
    RETURN g.Passable(tx + DirDX(d), ty + DirDY(d), pac)
END FUNCTION

' DistSq: Returns the SQUARED distance between two points.
' We use squared distance (no square root) because it's faster to compute
' and works fine for comparing "which is closer?" (if A^2 < B^2, then A < B).
FUNCTION DistSq(x1 AS INTEGER, y1 AS INTEGER, x2 AS INTEGER, y2 AS INTEGER) AS INTEGER
    DIM dx AS INTEGER = x1 - x2
    DIM dy AS INTEGER = y1 - y2
    RETURN dx * dx + dy * dy
END FUNCTION

' IAbs: Returns the absolute value (always positive) of a number.
' Example: IAbs(-5) = 5, IAbs(3) = 3
FUNCTION IAbs(x AS INTEGER) AS INTEGER
    IF x < 0 THEN RETURN -x
    RETURN x
END FUNCTION

' InTunnel: Checks if a tile position is inside the side tunnels.
' The tunnels are the passages on the far left and right of row 14.
' Ghosts move slower in tunnels (40% speed) but PacMan doesn't!
FUNCTION InTunnel(tx AS INTEGER, ty AS INTEGER) AS BOOLEAN
    IF ty <> TUNNEL_Y THEN RETURN FALSE
    IF tx < 6 THEN RETURN TRUE
    IF tx > 21 THEN RETURN TRUE
    RETURN FALSE
END FUNCTION

' PhaseDuration: Returns how many ticks each scatter/chase phase lasts.
' In the original PacMan, ghosts alternate between "scatter" (going to their
' corner) and "chase" (hunting PacMan). The pattern for Level 1 is:
'   7 seconds scatter -> 20 seconds chase -> 7s scatter -> 20s chase ->
'   5s scatter -> 20s chase -> 5s scatter -> chase FOREVER
FUNCTION PhaseDuration(phase AS INTEGER) AS INTEGER
    IF phase = 0 THEN RETURN 420
    IF phase = 1 THEN RETURN 1200
    IF phase = 2 THEN RETURN 420
    IF phase = 3 THEN RETURN 1200
    IF phase = 4 THEN RETURN 300
    IF phase = 5 THEN RETURN 1200
    IF phase = 6 THEN RETURN 300
    RETURN 99999
END FUNCTION

' PhaseMode: Even-numbered phases are scatter, odd-numbered are chase.
FUNCTION PhaseMode(phase AS INTEGER) AS INTEGER
    IF phase MOD 2 = 0 THEN RETURN M_SCATTER
    RETURN M_CHASE
END FUNCTION

' NearestPl: In co-op mode, ghosts target the NEAREST alive player.
' Returns the index (0 or 1) of the closest living player to the given position.
' If no players are alive, returns 0 as a fallback.
FUNCTION (g AS POINTER TO Game) NearestPl(gx AS INTEGER, gy AS INTEGER) AS INTEGER
    DIM best AS INTEGER = 0
    DIM bestD AS INTEGER = 999999
    DIM i AS INTEGER
    FOR i = 0 TO g.NumPl - 1
        IF g.Pl[i].Alive THEN
            DIM d AS INTEGER = DistSq(gx, gy, g.Pl[i].PX, g.Pl[i].PY)
            IF d < bestD THEN
                bestD = d
                best = i
            ENDIF
        ENDIF
    NEXT
    RETURN best
END FUNCTION

' ======================== HIGH SCORE MANAGEMENT ========================
' High scores are stored in a simple text file: each line has "AAA 12345"
' (3-letter initials, a space, then the score number).
' We keep the top 5 scores sorted from highest to lowest.

' LoadHiScores: Reads the high score file and returns up to 5 entries.
' If the file doesn't exist or is corrupt, returns a default list.
FUNCTION LoadHiScores() AS []HiEntry
    DIM scores AS []HiEntry
    DIM content AS STRING = ReadFile(HISCORE_FILE)
    IF LEN(content) = 0 THEN
        ' File doesn't exist yet or is empty - return defaults
        DIM j AS INTEGER
        FOR j = 0 TO MAX_HISCORES - 1
            DIM def AS HiEntry
            def.Initials = "---"
            def.Pts = 0
            scores = APPEND(scores, def)
        NEXT
        RETURN scores
    ENDIF

    ' Parse the file line by line
    DIM lines AS []STRING = strings.Split(content, Chr(10))
    DIM k AS INTEGER
    FOR k = 0 TO LEN(lines) - 1
        IF LEN(scores) >= MAX_HISCORES THEN
            ' We have enough entries, stop
            RETURN scores
        ENDIF
        DIM ln AS STRING = strings.TrimSpace(lines[k])
        IF LEN(ln) > 4 THEN
            ' Format: "AAA 12345"
            DIM initials AS STRING = Mid(ln, 1, 3)
            DIM numStr AS STRING = Mid(ln, 5, LEN(ln) - 4)
            DIM pts AS INTEGER
            DIM parseErr AS ERROR
            pts, parseErr = strconv.Atoi(numStr)
            IF parseErr = NIL THEN
                DIM entry AS HiEntry
                entry.Initials = initials
                entry.Pts = pts
                scores = APPEND(scores, entry)
            ENDIF
        ENDIF
    NEXT

    ' Pad with defaults if fewer than 5 entries
    DO WHILE LEN(scores) < MAX_HISCORES
        DIM pad AS HiEntry
        pad.Initials = "---"
        pad.Pts = 0
        scores = APPEND(scores, pad)
    LOOP

    RETURN scores
END FUNCTION

' SaveHiScores: Writes the high score table to the file.
SUB SaveHiScores(scores AS []HiEntry)
    DIM content AS STRING = ""
    DIM i AS INTEGER
    FOR i = 0 TO LEN(scores) - 1
        IF i >= MAX_HISCORES THEN
            WriteFile(HISCORE_FILE, content)
            RETURN
        ENDIF
        content = content & scores[i].Initials & " " & Str(scores[i].Pts) & Chr(10)
    NEXT
    WriteFile(HISCORE_FILE, content)
END SUB

' CheckHiScore: Returns the slot index (0-4) where this score should go,
' or -1 if it doesn't qualify for the top 5.
FUNCTION CheckHiScore(scores AS []HiEntry, pts AS INTEGER) AS INTEGER
    DIM i AS INTEGER
    FOR i = 0 TO LEN(scores) - 1
        IF i >= MAX_HISCORES THEN RETURN -1
        IF pts > scores[i].Pts THEN
            RETURN i
        ENDIF
    NEXT
    RETURN -1
END FUNCTION

' InsertHiScore: Inserts a new score at the given slot, shifting others down.
' Returns the updated list (still capped at MAX_HISCORES).
FUNCTION InsertHiScore(scores AS []HiEntry, slot AS INTEGER, entry AS HiEntry) AS []HiEntry
    DIM result AS []HiEntry
    DIM i AS INTEGER
    DIM inserted AS BOOLEAN = FALSE
    FOR i = 0 TO LEN(scores) - 1
        IF i = slot THEN
            IF NOT inserted THEN
                result = APPEND(result, entry)
                inserted = TRUE
            ENDIF
        ENDIF
        IF LEN(result) < MAX_HISCORES THEN
            result = APPEND(result, scores[i])
        ENDIF
    NEXT
    ' If slot is at the end
    IF NOT inserted THEN
        IF LEN(result) < MAX_HISCORES THEN
            result = APPEND(result, entry)
        ENDIF
    ENDIF
    ' Trim to MAX_HISCORES
    DIM trimmed AS []HiEntry
    DIM j AS INTEGER
    FOR j = 0 TO LEN(result) - 1
        IF j >= MAX_HISCORES THEN
            RETURN trimmed
        ENDIF
        trimmed = APPEND(trimmed, result[j])
    NEXT
    RETURN trimmed
END FUNCTION

' ======================== SOUND GENERATION ========================
' These functions create retro-style sound effects from pure math.
' We generate raw audio data (PCM) by computing a waveform one sample
' at a time, then hand that data to Ebitengine's audio player.
'
' PCM audio = a list of numbers that describe the sound wave's shape.
' Each number is a 16-bit integer (-32768 to 32767) representing how
' far the speaker cone should push out (positive) or pull in (negative).
' We need 44100 of these numbers per second (the "sample rate").
' Stereo means we need TWO numbers per sample (left + right ear).

' MakeTone: Generates a square-wave beep at a given frequency.
'   freq   = pitch in Hz (higher = squeakier, lower = deeper)
'   durMs  = duration in milliseconds
'   vol    = loudness (0-8000 is a good range)
' Returns raw PCM bytes ready for Ebitengine's audio player.
FUNCTION MakeTone(freq AS INTEGER, durMs AS INTEGER, vol AS INTEGER) AS STRING
    DIM rate AS INTEGER = 44100
    DIM samples AS INTEGER = rate * durMs / 1000
    DIM result AS STRING = ""
    DIM period AS INTEGER = rate / freq
    DIM half AS INTEGER = period / 2
    DIM i AS INTEGER
    DIM val AS INTEGER
    DIM uv AS INTEGER
    DIM lo AS INTEGER
    DIM hi AS INTEGER

    FOR i = 0 TO samples - 1
        ' Square wave: alternate between +vol and -vol
        val = vol
        IF (i MOD period) >= half THEN
            val = -vol
        ENDIF
        ' Decay envelope: sound fades out toward the end
        val = val * (samples - i) / samples

        ' Convert signed int16 to two bytes (little-endian)
        uv = val
        IF uv < 0 THEN
            uv = uv + 65536
        ENDIF
        lo = uv MOD 256
        hi = uv / 256
        ' Append one stereo sample (4 chars: lo+hi for left, lo+hi for right)
        result = result & Chr(lo) & Chr(hi) & Chr(lo) & Chr(hi)
    NEXT
    RETURN result
END FUNCTION

' MakeChirp: Generates a frequency sweep (ascending or descending).
'   startFreq = starting pitch
'   endFreq   = ending pitch
'   durMs     = duration in milliseconds
'   vol       = loudness
FUNCTION MakeChirp(startFreq AS INTEGER, endFreq AS INTEGER, durMs AS INTEGER, vol AS INTEGER) AS STRING
    DIM rate AS INTEGER = 44100
    DIM samples AS INTEGER = rate * durMs / 1000
    DIM result AS STRING = ""
    DIM i AS INTEGER
    DIM val AS INTEGER
    DIM uv AS INTEGER
    DIM lo AS INTEGER
    DIM hi AS INTEGER
    DIM freq AS INTEGER
    DIM period AS INTEGER
    DIM half AS INTEGER

    FOR i = 0 TO samples - 1
        ' Interpolate frequency from start to end
        freq = startFreq + (endFreq - startFreq) * i / samples
        period = rate / freq
        IF period < 1 THEN
            period = 1
        ENDIF
        half = period / 2

        val = vol
        IF (i MOD period) >= half THEN
            val = -vol
        ENDIF
        val = val * (samples - i) / samples

        uv = val
        IF uv < 0 THEN
            uv = uv + 65536
        ENDIF
        lo = uv MOD 256
        hi = uv / 256
        result = result & Chr(lo) & Chr(hi) & Chr(lo) & Chr(hi)
    NEXT
    RETURN result
END FUNCTION

' MakePlayer: Helper that creates an audio player from a PCM data string.
' Uses strings.NewReader (which implements io.ReadSeeker) to feed the data
' to Ebitengine's audio system.
FUNCTION MakePlayer(data AS STRING) AS POINTER TO audio.Player
    DIM reader AS POINTER TO strings.Reader = strings.NewReader(data)
    DIM player AS POINTER TO audio.Player
    DIM err AS ERROR
    player, err = GAudioCtx.NewPlayer(reader)
    IF err <> NIL THEN
        fmt.Println("Audio error:", err)
    ENDIF
    RETURN player
END FUNCTION

' InitSounds: Creates all the game's sound effects and stores them
' as audio players in the Game struct, ready to play.
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) InitSounds()
    ' Waka: short blip when eating a dot (classic PacMan sound)
    g.SndWaka = MakePlayer(MakeTone(440, 50, 3000))

    ' Power pellet: dramatic descending sweep
    g.SndPower = MakePlayer(MakeChirp(880, 220, 300, 4000))

    ' Eating a ghost: bright ascending chirp
    g.SndEatGh = MakePlayer(MakeChirp(330, 1200, 150, 3500))

    ' Death: sad descending tone
    g.SndDie = MakePlayer(MakeChirp(600, 100, 500, 4000))

    ' Ready jingle: quick ascending beep
    g.SndReady = MakePlayer(MakeChirp(330, 660, 200, 3000))

    ' Level won: triumphant ascending sweep
    g.SndWon = MakePlayer(MakeChirp(440, 1320, 400, 3500))

    ' Menu select: short blip for navigating the menu
    g.SndMenu = MakePlayer(MakeTone(660, 30, 2500))
END SUB

' PlaySound: Rewinds an audio player to the start and plays it.
' This lets us replay the same sound effect multiple times.
SUB PlaySound(snd AS POINTER TO audio.Player)
    IF snd <> NIL THEN
        snd.Rewind()
        snd.Play()
    ENDIF
END SUB

' ======================== PLAYER INITIALIZATION ========================
' Creates a fresh Player struct with starting values.

FUNCTION NewPlayer(colorIdx AS INTEGER) AS Player
    DIM p AS Player
    p.PX = T2P(PAC_SX)
    p.PY = T2P(PAC_SY)
    p.PDir = D_LEFT
    p.PNext = D_LEFT
    p.PMoveAcc = 0
    p.Mouth = TRUE
    p.MouthT = 0
    p.Score = 0
    p.Lives = 3
    p.IFrames = 0
    p.Alive = TRUE
    p.Clr = colorIdx
    RETURN p
END FUNCTION

' ======================== INITIALIZATION ========================
' NewGame creates a brand-new game from scratch. It sets up the maze,
' places PacMan and all 4 ghosts in their starting positions, and
' initializes the score, lives, and timers.
' The game starts on the INTRO (title/menu) screen.

FUNCTION NewGame() AS Game
    DIM g AS Game
    g.Level = 1
    g.State = S_INTRO
    g.MenuSel = 0
    g.GmMode = GM_SINGLE
    g.NumPl = 1
    g.CurPl = 0
    g.GMode = M_SCATTER
    g.MPhase = 0
    g.MTimer = PhaseDuration(0)
    g.GScore = 200

    ' Load high scores from file
    g.HiScores = LoadHiScores()

    ' We still build the maze and place ghosts so the title screen
    ' can show the maze in the background if we want.
    ' --- PARSE THE MAZE ---
    DIM layout AS []STRING = GetMazeLayout()
    g.Total = 0
    DIM x AS INTEGER
    DIM y AS INTEGER

    FOR y = 0 TO MH - 1
        FOR x = 0 TO MW - 1
            DIM ch AS STRING = Mid(layout[y], x + 1, 1)
            DIM cell AS INTEGER = C_EMPTY
            IF ch = "#" THEN
                cell = C_WALL
            ELSEIF ch = "." THEN
                cell = C_DOT
                g.Total = g.Total + 1
            ELSEIF ch = "o" THEN
                cell = C_POWER
                g.Total = g.Total + 1
            ELSEIF ch = "-" THEN
                cell = C_DOOR
            ENDIF
            g.Maze = APPEND(g.Maze, cell)
        NEXT
    NEXT

    ' --- CREATE PLAYER(S) ---
    ' Start with one player; we add the second when the player picks a mode.
    DIM p1 AS Player = NewPlayer(0)
    g.Pl = APPEND(g.Pl, p1)

    ' --- CREATE THE 4 GHOSTS ---
    ' Each ghost has a unique personality and starting position.
    '
    ' BLINKY (Red) - "Shadow"
    '   Starts outside the house, ready to chase immediately.
    '   Chase strategy: aims directly at PacMan's current tile.
    '   Scatter corner: top-right.
    DIM blinky AS Ghost
    blinky.X = T2P(14)
    blinky.Y = T2P(HOUSE_EXIT_Y)
    blinky.Dir = D_LEFT
    blinky.GType = 0
    blinky.Mode = M_SCATTER
    blinky.ScatX = MW - 3
    blinky.ScatY = 0
    g.Gh = APPEND(g.Gh, blinky)

    ' PINKY (Pink) - "Speedy"
    '   Starts inside the house, released almost immediately.
    '   Chase strategy: aims 4 tiles AHEAD of where PacMan is facing.
    '   Tries to ambush PacMan from the front!
    '   Scatter corner: top-left.
    DIM pinky AS Ghost
    pinky.X = T2P(HOUSE_CENTER_X)
    pinky.Y = T2P(HOUSE_CENTER_Y)
    pinky.Dir = D_UP
    pinky.GType = 1
    pinky.Mode = M_HOUSE
    pinky.ScatX = 2
    pinky.ScatY = 0
    g.Gh = APPEND(g.Gh, pinky)

    ' INKY (Cyan) - "Bashful"
    '   Starts inside the house, released after 30 dots eaten.
    '   Chase strategy: uses both PacMan's AND Blinky's positions
    '   to pick a target. This makes Inky unpredictable!
    '   Scatter corner: bottom-right.
    DIM inky AS Ghost
    inky.X = T2P(12)
    inky.Y = T2P(HOUSE_CENTER_Y)
    inky.Dir = D_UP
    inky.GType = 2
    inky.Mode = M_HOUSE
    inky.ScatX = MW - 1
    inky.ScatY = MH - 1
    g.Gh = APPEND(g.Gh, inky)

    ' CLYDE (Orange) - "Pokey"
    '   Starts inside the house, released after 60 dots eaten.
    '   Chase strategy: chases PacMan when far away, but gets shy and
    '   retreats to his corner when he gets close (within 8 tiles).
    '   Scatter corner: bottom-left.
    DIM clyde AS Ghost
    clyde.X = T2P(16)
    clyde.Y = T2P(HOUSE_CENTER_Y)
    clyde.Dir = D_UP
    clyde.GType = 3
    clyde.Mode = M_HOUSE
    clyde.ScatX = 0
    clyde.ScatY = MH - 1
    g.Gh = APPEND(g.Gh, clyde)

    ' --- PRE-RENDER WALLS ---
    g.WallImg = ebiten.NewImage(SCRW, SCRH)
    g.RenderWalls()
    g.InitSounds()

    RETURN g
END FUNCTION

' StartPlay: Called when the player selects a mode from the menu.
' Sets up the correct number of players and transitions to READY state.
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) StartPlay()
    g.GmMode = g.MenuSel
    g.State = S_READY
    g.STimer = T_READY
    g.CurPl = 0

    ' Reset player 1
    g.Pl[0] = NewPlayer(0)

    IF g.GmMode = GM_SINGLE THEN
        g.NumPl = 1
        ' Make sure we only have 1 player in the array
        DIM onePl AS []Player
        onePl = APPEND(onePl, g.Pl[0])
        g.Pl = onePl
    ELSE
        g.NumPl = 2
        DIM p2 AS Player = NewPlayer(1)
        ' For alternating, P2 starts at same position (they take turns)
        ' For co-op, P2 starts at a slightly different position
        IF g.GmMode = GM_COOP THEN
            p2.PX = T2P(14)
            p2.PY = T2P(PAC_SY)
        ENDIF
        DIM twoPl AS []Player
        twoPl = APPEND(twoPl, g.Pl[0])
        twoPl = APPEND(twoPl, p2)
        g.Pl = twoPl
    ENDIF

    ' Reset the maze (fresh dots)
    g.RebuildMaze()
    g.ResetPositions()

    ' For alternating mode, save the initial maze for both players
    IF g.GmMode = GM_ALTER THEN
        g.SaveAltMaze(0)
        g.SaveAltMaze(1)
    ENDIF
END SUB

' RebuildMaze: Re-reads the maze layout and resets all dots.
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) RebuildMaze()
    DIM layout AS []STRING = GetMazeLayout()
    DIM x AS INTEGER
    DIM y AS INTEGER
    g.Total = 0
    g.Eaten = 0

    ' Rebuild maze array from scratch
    DIM newMaze AS []INTEGER
    FOR y = 0 TO MH - 1
        FOR x = 0 TO MW - 1
            DIM ch AS STRING = Mid(layout[y], x + 1, 1)
            DIM cell AS INTEGER = C_EMPTY
            IF ch = "#" THEN
                cell = C_WALL
            ELSEIF ch = "." THEN
                cell = C_DOT
                g.Total = g.Total + 1
            ELSEIF ch = "o" THEN
                cell = C_POWER
                g.Total = g.Total + 1
            ELSEIF ch = "-" THEN
                cell = C_DOOR
            ENDIF
            newMaze = APPEND(newMaze, cell)
        NEXT
    NEXT
    g.Maze = newMaze

    g.WallImg.Clear()
    g.RenderWalls()
END SUB

' RenderWalls: Draws all the wall tiles and ghost house doors onto the
' cached wall image. This only runs once (or when starting a new level).
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) RenderWalls()
    DIM x AS INTEGER
    DIM y AS INTEGER
    FOR y = 0 TO MH - 1
        FOR x = 0 TO MW - 1
            DIM cell AS INTEGER = g.Maze[y * MW + x]
            DIM px AS INTEGER = x * TILE
            DIM py AS INTEGER = y * TILE + HUD_TOP
            IF cell = C_WALL THEN
                ' Draw a blue rectangle (slightly smaller than the tile for a grid effect)
                vector.DrawFilledRect(g.WallImg, Sng(px + 1), Sng(py + 1), Sng(TILE - 2), Sng(TILE - 2), color.RGBA{R: 33, G: 33, B: 255, A: 255}, FALSE)
            ELSEIF cell = C_DOOR THEN
                ' Draw a thin pink line for the ghost house door
                vector.DrawFilledRect(g.WallImg, Sng(px), Sng(py + TILE / 2 - 1), Sng(TILE), Sng(3), color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 184, B: 255, A: 255}, FALSE)
            ENDIF
        NEXT
    NEXT
END SUB

' ======================== ALTERNATING MODE HELPERS ========================
' In alternating mode, each player has their own maze state (which dots
' they've eaten). When we switch players, we save/restore the maze.

' SaveAltMaze: Saves the current maze state for the given player index.
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) SaveAltMaze(pIdx AS INTEGER)
    DIM copy AS []INTEGER
    DIM i AS INTEGER
    FOR i = 0 TO LEN(g.Maze) - 1
        copy = APPEND(copy, g.Maze[i])
    NEXT
    IF pIdx = 0 THEN
        g.AltMaze0 = copy
        g.AltEaten0 = g.Eaten
    ELSE
        g.AltMaze1 = copy
        g.AltEaten1 = g.Eaten
    ENDIF
END SUB

' RestoreAltMaze: Restores the maze state for the given player index.
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) RestoreAltMaze(pIdx AS INTEGER)
    DIM src AS []INTEGER
    IF pIdx = 0 THEN
        src = g.AltMaze0
        g.Eaten = g.AltEaten0
    ELSE
        src = g.AltMaze1
        g.Eaten = g.AltEaten1
    ENDIF
    IF LEN(src) > 0 THEN
        DIM i AS INTEGER
        FOR i = 0 TO LEN(src) - 1
            g.Maze[i] = src[i]
        NEXT
    ENDIF
    ' Recount total dots from the restored maze
    g.Total = 0
    DIM j AS INTEGER
    FOR j = 0 TO LEN(g.Maze) - 1
        IF g.Maze[j] = C_DOT THEN
            g.Total = g.Total + 1
        ELSEIF g.Maze[j] = C_POWER THEN
            g.Total = g.Total + 1
        ENDIF
    NEXT
    g.Total = g.Eaten + (g.Total)
    g.WallImg.Clear()
    g.RenderWalls()
END SUB

' ResetPositions: Called after PacMan dies (but still has lives left).
' Puts everyone back at their starting positions without resetting the
' maze or score - the dots you already ate stay eaten.
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) ResetPositions()
    ' Reset all players to starting position
    DIM pi AS INTEGER
    FOR pi = 0 TO g.NumPl - 1
        g.Pl[pi].PX = T2P(PAC_SX)
        g.Pl[pi].PY = T2P(PAC_SY)
        g.Pl[pi].PDir = D_LEFT
        g.Pl[pi].PNext = D_LEFT
        g.Pl[pi].PMoveAcc = 0
        g.Pl[pi].Mouth = TRUE
        g.Pl[pi].MouthT = 0
        g.Pl[pi].Alive = TRUE
    NEXT
    g.EPause = 0

    ' Blinky starts outside the house
    g.Gh[0].X = T2P(14)
    g.Gh[0].Y = T2P(HOUSE_EXIT_Y)
    g.Gh[0].Dir = D_LEFT
    g.Gh[0].Mode = M_SCATTER
    g.Gh[0].MoveAcc = 0

    ' Pinky, Inky, and Clyde start inside the house
    g.Gh[1].X = T2P(HOUSE_CENTER_X)
    g.Gh[1].Y = T2P(HOUSE_CENTER_Y)
    g.Gh[1].Dir = D_UP
    g.Gh[1].Mode = M_HOUSE
    g.Gh[1].MoveAcc = 0

    g.Gh[2].X = T2P(12)
    g.Gh[2].Y = T2P(HOUSE_CENTER_Y)
    g.Gh[2].Dir = D_UP
    g.Gh[2].Mode = M_HOUSE
    g.Gh[2].MoveAcc = 0

    g.Gh[3].X = T2P(16)
    g.Gh[3].Y = T2P(HOUSE_CENTER_Y)
    g.Gh[3].Dir = D_UP
    g.Gh[3].Mode = M_HOUSE
    g.Gh[3].MoveAcc = 0

    ' Reset the scatter/chase cycle
    g.GMode = M_SCATTER
    g.MPhase = 0
    g.MTimer = PhaseDuration(0)
    g.GScore = 200
END SUB

' NextLevel: Called when all dots are eaten. Refills the maze with
' fresh dots, bumps the level counter, and resets everyone's positions.
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) NextLevel()
    g.Level = g.Level + 1
    g.Eaten = 0

    ' Rebuild the maze from scratch (re-read the layout and place all dots)
    DIM layout AS []STRING = GetMazeLayout()
    DIM x AS INTEGER
    DIM y AS INTEGER
    g.Total = 0
    FOR y = 0 TO MH - 1
        FOR x = 0 TO MW - 1
            DIM ch AS STRING = Mid(layout[y], x + 1, 1)
            DIM cell AS INTEGER = C_EMPTY
            IF ch = "#" THEN
                cell = C_WALL
            ELSEIF ch = "." THEN
                cell = C_DOT
                g.Total = g.Total + 1
            ELSEIF ch = "o" THEN
                cell = C_POWER
                g.Total = g.Total + 1
            ELSEIF ch = "-" THEN
                cell = C_DOOR
            ENDIF
            g.Maze[y * MW + x] = cell
        NEXT
    NEXT

    ' Re-render walls and reset positions
    g.WallImg.Clear()
    g.RenderWalls()
    g.ResetPositions()
    g.State = S_READY
    g.STimer = T_READY

    ' For alternating mode, save both maze states
    IF g.GmMode = GM_ALTER THEN
        g.SaveAltMaze(0)
        g.SaveAltMaze(1)
    ENDIF
END SUB

' ======================== SPEED HELPERS ========================

' GetPacSpeed: Returns PacMan's current speed percentage.
' PacMan moves faster when ghosts are frightened (he's more confident!).
FUNCTION (g AS POINTER TO Game) GetPacSpeed() AS INTEGER
    DIM i AS INTEGER
    DIM anyFright AS BOOLEAN = FALSE
    FOR i = 0 TO 3
        IF g.Gh[i].Mode = M_FRIGHT THEN
            anyFright = TRUE
        ENDIF
    NEXT
    IF anyFright THEN RETURN SPD_FRIGHT_PAC
    RETURN SPD_PAC
END FUNCTION

' GetGhostSpeed: Returns a ghost's speed based on what it's doing.
' - Eaten (eyes only): VERY fast (150%) - rushes back to the house
' - Entering/leaving house: slow (30%)
' - Waiting in house: 0 (frozen)
' - Frightened: slow (50%) - easy for PacMan to catch
' - In tunnel: slow (40%) - this is why tunnels are safe escape routes!
' - Normal: 75% - slightly slower than PacMan
FUNCTION (g AS POINTER TO Game) GetGhostSpeed(idx AS INTEGER) AS INTEGER
    DIM mode AS INTEGER = g.Gh[idx].Mode
    IF mode = M_EATEN THEN RETURN SPD_EYES
    IF mode = M_ENTER THEN RETURN SPD_HOUSE
    IF mode = M_LEAVE THEN RETURN SPD_HOUSE
    IF mode = M_HOUSE THEN RETURN 0
    IF mode = M_FRIGHT THEN RETURN SPD_FRIGHT_GHOST
    DIM tx AS INTEGER = P2T(g.Gh[idx].X)
    DIM ty AS INTEGER = P2T(g.Gh[idx].Y)
    IF InTunnel(tx, ty) THEN RETURN SPD_TUNNEL
    RETURN SPD_GHOST
END FUNCTION

' ======================== GAME LOGIC (Update) ========================
' This is the HEART of the game. It runs 60 times per second and handles
' ALL the game logic: input, movement, collisions, scoring, and state changes.
'
' The game engine (Ebitengine) calls Update() automatically every tick.
' We must return NIL (no error) to keep the game running.

FUNCTION (g AS POINTER TO Game) Update() AS ERROR
    g.Frame = g.Frame + 1

    ' --- GAME STATE MACHINE ---
    ' The game can be in different states. We handle each one differently.
    ' This is called a "state machine" - a very common pattern in games.
    SELECT CASE g.State

        CASE S_INTRO
            ' Title/menu screen. Player picks a mode with Up/Down + Enter.
            g.UpdateIntro()
            RETURN NIL

        CASE S_HISCORE
            ' High score initials entry screen.
            g.UpdateHiScore()
            RETURN NIL

        CASE S_READY
            ' Show "READY!" for 2 seconds before the game starts
            ' Play the ready jingle on the first tick
            IF g.STimer = T_READY THEN
                PlaySound(g.SndReady)
            ENDIF
            g.STimer = g.STimer - 1
            IF g.STimer <= 0 THEN
                g.State = S_PLAY
            ENDIF
            RETURN NIL

        CASE S_DYING
            ' PacMan's death animation (1 second of flashing)
            g.STimer = g.STimer - 1
            IF g.STimer <= 0 THEN
                g.HandleDeath()
            ENDIF
            RETURN NIL

        CASE S_OVER
            ' Game Over - wait for player to press Enter to check high scores
            IF inpututil.IsKeyJustPressed(ebiten.KeyEnter) THEN
                g.TransitionFromGameOver()
            ENDIF
            RETURN NIL

        CASE S_WON
            ' Level complete! Short celebration, then load next level
            g.STimer = g.STimer - 1
            IF g.STimer <= 0 THEN
                g.NextLevel()
            ENDIF
            RETURN NIL
    END SELECT

    ' --- PLAYING STATE ---
    ' If we reach here, the game is actively being played.

    ' Step 1: Check what keys the player(s) are pressing
    g.HandleInput()

    ' Step 2: "Eat pause" - when PacMan eats a dot, there's a tiny pause.
    ' This is authentic to the original game and makes dot-eating feel satisfying.
    ' During the pause, ghosts still move (giving them a slight advantage).
    IF g.EPause > 0 THEN
        g.EPause = g.EPause - 1
        g.MoveGhosts()
        g.UpdateMode()
        RETURN NIL
    ENDIF

    ' Step 3: Move player(s) depending on game mode
    IF g.GmMode = GM_COOP THEN
        ' Co-op: move both players
        DIM ci AS INTEGER
        FOR ci = 0 TO g.NumPl - 1
            IF g.Pl[ci].Alive THEN
                g.MovePlayer(ci)
            ENDIF
        NEXT
    ELSE
        ' Single or alternating: move the current player
        g.MovePlayer(g.CurPl)
    ENDIF

    g.MoveGhosts()

    ' Step 4: Check for collisions (PacMan touching dots or ghosts)
    IF g.GmMode = GM_COOP THEN
        DIM di AS INTEGER
        FOR di = 0 TO g.NumPl - 1
            IF g.Pl[di].Alive THEN
                g.CheckDotsFor(di)
                g.CheckGhostsFor(di)
            ENDIF
        NEXT
    ELSE
        g.CheckDotsFor(g.CurPl)
        g.CheckGhostsFor(g.CurPl)
    ENDIF

    ' Step 5: Update the scatter/chase timer
    g.UpdateMode()

    ' Step 6: Animate PacMan's mouth (open/close every 6 ticks) for all players
    DIM mi AS INTEGER
    FOR mi = 0 TO g.NumPl - 1
        IF g.Pl[mi].Alive THEN
            ' Mouth animation: cycle through 16 frames continuously
            ' 0-3: closed, 4-7: half open, 8-11: full open, 12-15: half open
            g.Pl[mi].MouthT = (g.Pl[mi].MouthT + 1) MOD 16
        ENDIF
    NEXT

    RETURN NIL
END FUNCTION

' ======================== INTRO / MENU UPDATE ========================
' The title screen shows the game name and a menu of game modes.
' Player navigates with Up/Down arrows and presses Enter to select.

SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) UpdateIntro()
    IF inpututil.IsKeyJustPressed(ebiten.KeyArrowUp) THEN
        g.MenuSel = g.MenuSel - 1
        IF g.MenuSel < 0 THEN
            g.MenuSel = 2
        ENDIF
        PlaySound(g.SndMenu)
    ELSEIF inpututil.IsKeyJustPressed(ebiten.KeyArrowDown) THEN
        g.MenuSel = g.MenuSel + 1
        IF g.MenuSel > 2 THEN
            g.MenuSel = 0
        ENDIF
        PlaySound(g.SndMenu)
    ENDIF

    IF inpututil.IsKeyJustPressed(ebiten.KeyEnter) THEN
        PlaySound(g.SndReady)
        g.StartPlay()
    ENDIF
END SUB

' ======================== HIGH SCORE ENTRY UPDATE ========================
' After game over, if a player qualifies for the top 5, they enter 3-letter
' initials. Up/Down changes the current letter, Left/Right moves between
' the 3 letter positions, Enter confirms.

SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) UpdateHiScore()
    ' Determine which player is currently entering initials
    DIM activeP AS INTEGER = g.HiPlIdx

    IF inpututil.IsKeyJustPressed(ebiten.KeyArrowUp) THEN
        g.HiName[g.HiCursor] = g.HiName[g.HiCursor] + 1
        IF g.HiName[g.HiCursor] > 25 THEN
            g.HiName[g.HiCursor] = 0
        ENDIF
        PlaySound(g.SndMenu)
    ELSEIF inpututil.IsKeyJustPressed(ebiten.KeyArrowDown) THEN
        g.HiName[g.HiCursor] = g.HiName[g.HiCursor] - 1
        IF g.HiName[g.HiCursor] < 0 THEN
            g.HiName[g.HiCursor] = 25
        ENDIF
        PlaySound(g.SndMenu)
    ENDIF

    IF inpututil.IsKeyJustPressed(ebiten.KeyArrowRight) THEN
        g.HiCursor = g.HiCursor + 1
        IF g.HiCursor > 2 THEN
            g.HiCursor = 2
        ENDIF
    ELSEIF inpututil.IsKeyJustPressed(ebiten.KeyArrowLeft) THEN
        g.HiCursor = g.HiCursor - 1
        IF g.HiCursor < 0 THEN
            g.HiCursor = 0
        ENDIF
    ENDIF

    IF inpututil.IsKeyJustPressed(ebiten.KeyEnter) THEN
        ' Build the 3-letter string from the letter codes
        DIM initials AS STRING = Chr(g.HiName[0] + 65) & Chr(g.HiName[1] + 65) & Chr(g.HiName[2] + 65)
        DIM entry AS HiEntry
        entry.Initials = initials
        entry.Pts = g.Pl[activeP].Score
        g.HiScores = InsertHiScore(g.HiScores, g.HiSlot, entry)
        SaveHiScores(g.HiScores)
        PlaySound(g.SndWon)

        ' Mark this player as done
        IF activeP = 0 THEN
            g.HiDone0 = TRUE
        ELSE
            g.HiDone1 = TRUE
        ENDIF

        ' Check if the other player also qualifies (2-player modes)
        IF g.NumPl > 1 THEN
            DIM otherP AS INTEGER = 1 - activeP
            DIM alreadyDone AS BOOLEAN = FALSE
            IF otherP = 0 THEN
                alreadyDone = g.HiDone0
            ELSE
                alreadyDone = g.HiDone1
            ENDIF
            IF NOT alreadyDone THEN
                DIM slot2 AS INTEGER = CheckHiScore(g.HiScores, g.Pl[otherP].Score)
                IF slot2 >= 0 THEN
                    ' Other player qualifies too! Set up entry for them.
                    g.HiPlIdx = otherP
                    g.HiSlot = slot2
                    g.HiCursor = 0
                    g.HiName[0] = 0
                    g.HiName[1] = 0
                    g.HiName[2] = 0
                    RETURN
                ENDIF
            ENDIF
        ENDIF

        ' All done - go back to intro
        g.State = S_INTRO
        g.MenuSel = 0
    ENDIF
END SUB

' ======================== DEATH HANDLING ========================
' When a player dies, different things happen based on game mode.

SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) HandleDeath()
    IF g.GmMode = GM_SINGLE THEN
        ' Single player: lose a life, game over if none left
        g.Pl[0].Lives = g.Pl[0].Lives - 1
        IF g.Pl[0].Lives <= 0 THEN
            g.State = S_OVER
        ELSE
            g.ResetPositions()
            g.State = S_READY
            g.STimer = T_READY
        ENDIF

    ELSEIF g.GmMode = GM_ALTER THEN
        ' Alternating: current player loses a life
        DIM cp AS INTEGER = g.CurPl
        g.Pl[cp].Lives = g.Pl[cp].Lives - 1

        ' Save this player's maze state
        g.SaveAltMaze(cp)

        ' Check if both players are out of lives
        DIM bothDead AS BOOLEAN = FALSE
        IF g.Pl[0].Lives <= 0 THEN
            IF g.Pl[1].Lives <= 0 THEN
                bothDead = TRUE
            ENDIF
        ENDIF

        IF bothDead THEN
            g.State = S_OVER
        ELSE
            ' Switch to the other player if they have lives
            DIM otherP AS INTEGER = 1 - cp
            IF g.Pl[otherP].Lives > 0 THEN
                g.CurPl = otherP
                g.RestoreAltMaze(otherP)
            ENDIF
            ' If other player is also dead, stay with current
            ' (they still have lives since bothDead was false)
            g.ResetPositions()
            g.State = S_READY
            g.STimer = T_READY
        ENDIF

    ELSEIF g.GmMode = GM_COOP THEN
        ' Co-op: the dying player loses a life
        DIM dp AS INTEGER = g.AltDying
        g.Pl[dp].Lives = g.Pl[dp].Lives - 1
        IF g.Pl[dp].Lives <= 0 THEN
            g.Pl[dp].Alive = FALSE
        ENDIF

        ' Check if ALL players are out of lives
        DIM allDead AS BOOLEAN = TRUE
        DIM ci AS INTEGER
        FOR ci = 0 TO g.NumPl - 1
            IF g.Pl[ci].Lives > 0 THEN
                allDead = FALSE
            ENDIF
        NEXT

        IF allDead THEN
            g.State = S_OVER
        ELSE
            g.ResetPositions()
            ' Mark dead players as not alive
            DIM ri AS INTEGER
            FOR ri = 0 TO g.NumPl - 1
                IF g.Pl[ri].Lives <= 0 THEN
                    g.Pl[ri].Alive = FALSE
                ENDIF
            NEXT
            g.State = S_READY
            g.STimer = T_READY
        ENDIF
    ENDIF
END SUB

' TransitionFromGameOver: Called when player presses Enter on Game Over screen.
' Checks if any player qualifies for the high score table.
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) TransitionFromGameOver()
    g.HiDone0 = FALSE
    g.HiDone1 = FALSE

    ' Check each player's score against the high score table
    DIM pi AS INTEGER
    FOR pi = 0 TO g.NumPl - 1
        DIM slot AS INTEGER = CheckHiScore(g.HiScores, g.Pl[pi].Score)
        IF slot >= 0 THEN
            ' This player qualifies! Enter initials.
            g.State = S_HISCORE
            g.HiPlIdx = pi
            g.HiSlot = slot
            g.HiCursor = 0
            ' Initialize the 3 letter slots to 'A' (code 0)
            DIM letters AS []INTEGER
            letters = APPEND(letters, 0)
            letters = APPEND(letters, 0)
            letters = APPEND(letters, 0)
            g.HiName = letters
            IF pi = 0 THEN
                g.HiDone0 = FALSE
            ELSE
                g.HiDone1 = FALSE
            ENDIF
            RETURN
        ENDIF
    NEXT

    ' No one qualifies - go back to intro
    g.State = S_INTRO
    g.MenuSel = 0
END SUB

' HandleInput: Reads the keyboard and remembers what direction the player(s)
' want PacMan to go. PacMan won't actually turn until he reaches a tile
' center where that direction is valid (no wall in the way).
'
' In co-op: P1 uses WASD, P2 uses Arrow keys.
' In single/alternating: both WASD and Arrows control the active player.
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) HandleInput()
    IF g.GmMode = GM_COOP THEN
        ' --- CO-OP INPUT ---
        ' Player 1: WASD
        IF ebiten.IsKeyPressed(ebiten.KeyW) THEN
            g.Pl[0].PNext = D_UP
        ELSEIF ebiten.IsKeyPressed(ebiten.KeyS) THEN
            g.Pl[0].PNext = D_DOWN
        ELSEIF ebiten.IsKeyPressed(ebiten.KeyA) THEN
            g.Pl[0].PNext = D_LEFT
        ELSEIF ebiten.IsKeyPressed(ebiten.KeyD) THEN
            g.Pl[0].PNext = D_RIGHT
        ENDIF
        ' Player 2: Arrow keys
        IF ebiten.IsKeyPressed(ebiten.KeyArrowUp) THEN
            g.Pl[1].PNext = D_UP
        ELSEIF ebiten.IsKeyPressed(ebiten.KeyArrowDown) THEN
            g.Pl[1].PNext = D_DOWN
        ELSEIF ebiten.IsKeyPressed(ebiten.KeyArrowLeft) THEN
            g.Pl[1].PNext = D_LEFT
        ELSEIF ebiten.IsKeyPressed(ebiten.KeyArrowRight) THEN
            g.Pl[1].PNext = D_RIGHT
        ENDIF
    ELSE
        ' --- SINGLE / ALTERNATING INPUT ---
        ' Both WASD and Arrows control the active player.
        DIM cp AS INTEGER = g.CurPl
        IF ebiten.IsKeyPressed(ebiten.KeyArrowUp) THEN
            g.Pl[cp].PNext = D_UP
        ELSEIF ebiten.IsKeyPressed(ebiten.KeyW) THEN
            g.Pl[cp].PNext = D_UP
        ELSEIF ebiten.IsKeyPressed(ebiten.KeyArrowDown) THEN
            g.Pl[cp].PNext = D_DOWN
        ELSEIF ebiten.IsKeyPressed(ebiten.KeyS) THEN
            g.Pl[cp].PNext = D_DOWN
        ELSEIF ebiten.IsKeyPressed(ebiten.KeyArrowLeft) THEN
            g.Pl[cp].PNext = D_LEFT
        ELSEIF ebiten.IsKeyPressed(ebiten.KeyA) THEN
            g.Pl[cp].PNext = D_LEFT
        ELSEIF ebiten.IsKeyPressed(ebiten.KeyArrowRight) THEN
            g.Pl[cp].PNext = D_RIGHT
        ELSEIF ebiten.IsKeyPressed(ebiten.KeyD) THEN
            g.Pl[cp].PNext = D_RIGHT
        ENDIF
    ENDIF
END SUB

' MovePlayer: Handles movement for a single player using the accumulator
' speed system. This replaces the old MovePacMan function.
'
' The movement logic:
'   1. Add speed to accumulator. If under 100, skip this frame (no movement).
'   2. If at a tile center, check if the player's desired direction is valid.
'      If so, turn that way. If current direction hits a wall, stop.
'   3. Move 2 pixels in the current direction.
'   4. Handle tunnel wrapping (going off the left edge appears on the right).
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) MovePlayer(pIdx AS INTEGER)
    ' --- ACCUMULATOR SPEED CHECK ---
    DIM spd AS INTEGER = g.GetPacSpeed()
    g.Pl[pIdx].PMoveAcc = g.Pl[pIdx].PMoveAcc + spd
    IF g.Pl[pIdx].PMoveAcc < 100 THEN RETURN
    g.Pl[pIdx].PMoveAcc = g.Pl[pIdx].PMoveAcc - 100

    ' --- DIRECTION DECISIONS (only at tile centers) ---
    DIM tx AS INTEGER = P2T(g.Pl[pIdx].PX)
    DIM ty AS INTEGER = P2T(g.Pl[pIdx].PY)

    IF AtCenter(g.Pl[pIdx].PX, g.Pl[pIdx].PY) THEN
        ' Try to turn in the direction the player wants
        IF g.Pl[pIdx].PNext <> D_NONE THEN
            IF g.CanGo(tx, ty, g.Pl[pIdx].PNext, TRUE) THEN
                g.Pl[pIdx].PDir = g.Pl[pIdx].PNext
            ENDIF
        ENDIF
        ' If current direction hits a wall, stop moving
        DIM canContinue AS BOOLEAN = g.CanGo(tx, ty, g.Pl[pIdx].PDir, TRUE)
        IF canContinue = FALSE THEN
            g.Pl[pIdx].PDir = D_NONE
        ENDIF
    ENDIF

    ' --- ACTUALLY MOVE ---
    IF g.Pl[pIdx].PDir <> D_NONE THEN
        g.Pl[pIdx].PX = g.Pl[pIdx].PX + DirDX(g.Pl[pIdx].PDir) * PX_STEP
        g.Pl[pIdx].PY = g.Pl[pIdx].PY + DirDY(g.Pl[pIdx].PDir) * PX_STEP
    ENDIF

    ' --- TUNNEL WRAPPING ---
    ' If PacMan goes off the left edge, appear on the right (and vice versa).
    IF g.Pl[pIdx].PX < 0 THEN
        g.Pl[pIdx].PX = g.Pl[pIdx].PX + MW * TILE
    ELSEIF g.Pl[pIdx].PX >= MW * TILE THEN
        g.Pl[pIdx].PX = g.Pl[pIdx].PX - MW * TILE
    ENDIF
END SUB

' CheckDotsFor: When a specific player's PacMan is at a tile center,
' check if there's a dot or power pellet on that tile. If so, eat it!
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) CheckDotsFor(pIdx AS INTEGER)
    IF NOT AtCenter(g.Pl[pIdx].PX, g.Pl[pIdx].PY) THEN RETURN

    DIM tx AS INTEGER = P2T(g.Pl[pIdx].PX)
    DIM ty AS INTEGER = P2T(g.Pl[pIdx].PY)
    IF tx < 0 OR tx >= MW OR ty < 0 OR ty >= MH THEN RETURN

    DIM cell AS INTEGER = g.Maze[ty * MW + tx]
    IF cell = C_DOT THEN
        ' Eat the dot: remove it from the maze, add 10 points
        g.Maze[ty * MW + tx] = C_EMPTY
        g.Pl[pIdx].Score = g.Pl[pIdx].Score + 10
        g.Eaten = g.Eaten + 1
        g.EPause = 1
        g.ReleaseGhosts()
        PlaySound(g.SndWaka)
    ELSEIF cell = C_POWER THEN
        ' Eat the power pellet: 50 points AND scare all the ghosts!
        g.Maze[ty * MW + tx] = C_EMPTY
        g.Pl[pIdx].Score = g.Pl[pIdx].Score + 50
        g.Eaten = g.Eaten + 1
        g.EPause = 3
        g.FrightenAll()
        g.ReleaseGhosts()
        PlaySound(g.SndPower)
    ENDIF

    ' Check if all dots are eaten - level complete!
    IF g.Eaten >= g.Total THEN
        g.State = S_WON
        g.STimer = 120
        PlaySound(g.SndWon)
    ENDIF
END SUB

' CheckGhostsFor: Check if a specific player's PacMan is touching any ghost.
' Uses pixel-distance collision (not just tile matching) for accuracy.
'
' Three possible outcomes when PacMan touches a ghost:
'   1. Ghost is FRIGHTENED -> PacMan eats the ghost! Score multiplies.
'   2. Ghost is EATEN (eyes) -> Nothing happens, they pass through.
'   3. Ghost is normal -> PacMan DIES!
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) CheckGhostsFor(pIdx AS INTEGER)
    DIM i AS INTEGER
    FOR i = 0 TO 3
        ' Skip ghosts that are in the house or transitioning
        IF g.Gh[i].Mode = M_HOUSE THEN
            ' skip
        ELSEIF g.Gh[i].Mode = M_ENTER THEN
            ' skip
        ELSEIF g.Gh[i].Mode = M_LEAVE THEN
            ' skip
        ELSE
            ' Calculate pixel distance between PacMan and this ghost
            DIM dx AS INTEGER = IAbs(g.Pl[pIdx].PX - g.Gh[i].X)
            DIM dy AS INTEGER = IAbs(g.Pl[pIdx].PY - g.Gh[i].Y)
            ' Account for tunnel wrap (if they're on opposite sides of the screen)
            IF dx > MW * TILE / 2 THEN
                dx = MW * TILE - dx
            ENDIF
            ' If within 12 pixels on both axes, they're touching
            IF dx < TILE - 4 THEN
                IF dy < TILE - 4 THEN
                    IF g.Gh[i].Mode = M_FRIGHT THEN
                        ' PacMan eats the ghost! The ghost becomes just eyes.
                        g.Gh[i].Mode = M_EATEN
                        g.Gh[i].MoveAcc = 0
                        g.Pl[pIdx].Score = g.Pl[pIdx].Score + g.GScore
                        ' Ghost score doubles: 200, 400, 800, 1600
                        g.GScore = g.GScore * 2
                        PlaySound(g.SndEatGh)
                    ELSEIF g.Gh[i].Mode <> M_EATEN THEN
                        ' PacMan touched a normal ghost - he dies!
                        g.AltDying = pIdx
                        g.State = S_DYING
                        g.STimer = T_DYING
                        PlaySound(g.SndDie)
                        RETURN
                    ENDIF
                ENDIF
            ENDIF
        ENDIF
    NEXT
END SUB

' FrightenAll: Called when PacMan eats a power pellet.
' All ghosts that are currently in scatter or chase mode become frightened.
' They turn blue, slow down, and run in random directions.
' PacMan can eat them for bonus points!
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) FrightenAll()
    ' Reset the ghost-eating score multiplier
    g.GScore = 200
    DIM i AS INTEGER
    FOR i = 0 TO 3
        IF g.Gh[i].Mode = M_SCATTER OR g.Gh[i].Mode = M_CHASE THEN
            g.Gh[i].Mode = M_FRIGHT
            g.Gh[i].FTimer = T_FRIGHT
            ' Ghosts immediately reverse direction when frightened!
            g.Gh[i].Dir = Opposite(g.Gh[i].Dir)
            g.Gh[i].MoveAcc = 0
        ENDIF
    NEXT
END SUB

' ReleaseGhosts: Check if any ghosts in the house should be released.
' Each ghost has a dot threshold - once PacMan eats that many dots,
' the ghost starts leaving the house.
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) ReleaseGhosts()
    DIM i AS INTEGER
    FOR i = 0 TO 3
        IF g.Gh[i].Mode = M_HOUSE THEN
            DIM thresh AS INTEGER = 999
            IF g.Gh[i].GType = 1 THEN
                thresh = REL_PINKY
            ELSEIF g.Gh[i].GType = 2 THEN
                thresh = REL_INKY
            ELSEIF g.Gh[i].GType = 3 THEN
                thresh = REL_CLYDE
            ENDIF
            IF g.Eaten >= thresh THEN
                ' Time to leave! Ghost starts the exit procedure.
                g.Gh[i].Mode = M_LEAVE
                g.Gh[i].X = T2P(HOUSE_CENTER_X)
                g.Gh[i].Dir = D_UP
                g.Gh[i].MoveAcc = 0
            ENDIF
        ENDIF
    NEXT
END SUB

' UpdateMode: Manages two timing systems:
'   1. Individual ghost frighten timers (count down to un-frighten)
'   2. The global scatter/chase cycle (alternates between the two modes)
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) UpdateMode()
    DIM i AS INTEGER

    ' --- FRIGHTEN TIMERS ---
    ' Each frightened ghost counts down. When the timer hits zero,
    ' the ghost goes back to whatever the current global mode is.
    FOR i = 0 TO 3
        IF g.Gh[i].Mode = M_FRIGHT THEN
            g.Gh[i].FTimer = g.Gh[i].FTimer - 1
            IF g.Gh[i].FTimer <= 0 THEN
                g.Gh[i].Mode = g.GMode
            ENDIF
        ENDIF
    NEXT

    ' --- SCATTER/CHASE CYCLE ---
    ' The game alternates between scatter and chase phases.
    ' When the mode switches, all active ghosts reverse direction.
    g.MTimer = g.MTimer - 1
    IF g.MTimer <= 0 THEN
        g.MPhase = g.MPhase + 1
        g.GMode = PhaseMode(g.MPhase)
        g.MTimer = PhaseDuration(g.MPhase)
        ' All active ghosts switch to the new mode and turn around
        FOR i = 0 TO 3
            IF g.Gh[i].Mode = M_SCATTER OR g.Gh[i].Mode = M_CHASE THEN
                g.Gh[i].Mode = g.GMode
                g.Gh[i].Dir = Opposite(g.Gh[i].Dir)
            ENDIF
        NEXT
    ENDIF
END SUB

' ======================== GHOST AI (Artificial Intelligence) ========================
' This is the most complex part of the game! Each ghost has to decide
' which direction to turn at every intersection.
'
' THE GHOST LIFECYCLE:
'   1. Start in the HOUSE (jail), waiting to be released
'   2. LEAVE the house (float up through the door)
'   3. Alternate between SCATTER (go to corner) and CHASE (hunt PacMan)
'   4. If PacMan eats a power pellet: become FRIGHTENED (run randomly)
'   5. If PacMan eats you while frightened: become EATEN (eyes only)
'   6. Race back to the house as eyes, ENTER the house, regenerate
'   7. LEAVE the house again and go back to step 3

' MoveGhosts: Main ghost movement handler. Routes each ghost to the
' appropriate movement function based on its current mode.
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) MoveGhosts()
    DIM i AS INTEGER
    FOR i = 0 TO 3
        IF g.Gh[i].Mode = M_HOUSE THEN
            ' Ghost is sitting in the house, waiting to be released.
            ' It doesn't move (just bobs in place visually).
        ELSEIF g.Gh[i].Mode = M_ENTER THEN
            ' Ghost eyes are floating DOWN into the house after being eaten
            g.MoveGhostEntering(i)
        ELSEIF g.Gh[i].Mode = M_LEAVE THEN
            ' Ghost is floating UP out of the house to rejoin the game
            g.MoveGhostLeaving(i)
        ELSE
            ' --- NORMAL GHOST MOVEMENT (scatter, chase, frightened, or eaten eyes) ---
            ' Uses the same accumulator speed system as PacMan
            DIM spd AS INTEGER = g.GetGhostSpeed(i)
            g.Gh[i].MoveAcc = g.Gh[i].MoveAcc + spd
            IF g.Gh[i].MoveAcc >= 100 THEN
                g.Gh[i].MoveAcc = g.Gh[i].MoveAcc - 100

                ' --- DIRECTION DECISION (at tile centers only) ---
                IF AtCenter(g.Gh[i].X, g.Gh[i].Y) THEN
                    DIM gtx AS INTEGER = P2T(g.Gh[i].X)
                    DIM gty AS INTEGER = P2T(g.Gh[i].Y)

                    ' If this ghost is just eyes (eaten), check if it reached
                    ' the ghost house door. If so, start entering the house.
                    IF g.Gh[i].Mode = M_EATEN THEN
                        IF gtx >= 13 THEN
                            IF gtx <= 15 THEN
                                IF gty = HOUSE_DOOR_Y THEN
                                    g.Gh[i].Mode = M_ENTER
                                    g.Gh[i].X = T2P(HOUSE_CENTER_X)
                                    g.Gh[i].Y = T2P(HOUSE_DOOR_Y)
                                    g.Gh[i].Dir = D_DOWN
                                    g.Gh[i].MoveAcc = 0
                                ENDIF
                            ENDIF
                        ENDIF
                    ENDIF

                    ' Use AI to choose the best direction (unless entering house)
                    IF g.Gh[i].Mode <> M_ENTER THEN
                        g.ChooseDir(i)
                    ENDIF
                ENDIF

                ' --- MOVE THE GHOST ---
                IF g.Gh[i].Mode <> M_ENTER THEN
                    g.Gh[i].X = g.Gh[i].X + DirDX(g.Gh[i].Dir) * PX_STEP
                    g.Gh[i].Y = g.Gh[i].Y + DirDY(g.Gh[i].Dir) * PX_STEP
                ENDIF

                ' --- TUNNEL WRAPPING ---
                IF g.Gh[i].X < 0 THEN
                    g.Gh[i].X = g.Gh[i].X + MW * TILE
                ELSEIF g.Gh[i].X >= MW * TILE THEN
                    g.Gh[i].X = g.Gh[i].X - MW * TILE
                ENDIF

                ' Eyes move at 150% speed, so they might get two moves per tick.
                ' This extra check handles that.
                IF g.Gh[i].Mode = M_EATEN THEN
                    IF g.Gh[i].MoveAcc >= 100 THEN
                        g.Gh[i].MoveAcc = g.Gh[i].MoveAcc - 100
                        g.Gh[i].X = g.Gh[i].X + DirDX(g.Gh[i].Dir) * PX_STEP
                        g.Gh[i].Y = g.Gh[i].Y + DirDY(g.Gh[i].Dir) * PX_STEP
                    ENDIF
                ENDIF
            ENDIF
        ENDIF
    NEXT
END SUB

' MoveGhostEntering: After a ghost is eaten, its eyes travel back to the
' ghost house. When they arrive at the door, this function takes over.
' The eyes float DOWN into the center of the house, then the ghost
' regenerates (gets its body back) after a brief pause.
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) MoveGhostEntering(idx AS INTEGER)
    DIM spd AS INTEGER = SPD_HOUSE
    g.Gh[idx].MoveAcc = g.Gh[idx].MoveAcc + spd
    IF g.Gh[idx].MoveAcc < 100 THEN RETURN
    g.Gh[idx].MoveAcc = g.Gh[idx].MoveAcc - 100

    ' Float down toward the center of the ghost house
    g.Gh[idx].Y = g.Gh[idx].Y + PX_STEP

    ' Did we reach the center? If so, regenerate and prepare to leave.
    DIM targetY AS INTEGER = T2P(HOUSE_CENTER_Y)
    IF g.Gh[idx].Y >= targetY THEN
        g.Gh[idx].Y = targetY
        ' Switch to LEAVE mode with a half-second pause to "regenerate"
        g.Gh[idx].Mode = M_LEAVE
        g.Gh[idx].Dir = D_UP
        g.Gh[idx].HouseTimer = 30
        g.Gh[idx].MoveAcc = 0
    ENDIF
END SUB

' MoveGhostLeaving: Handles a ghost exiting the ghost house.
' Three steps: 1) Wait out the house timer, 2) Slide to center X,
' 3) Float up through the door. Once above the door, rejoin the game.
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) MoveGhostLeaving(idx AS INTEGER)
    ' Step 1: Wait if there's a pause timer (regeneration time)
    IF g.Gh[idx].HouseTimer > 0 THEN
        g.Gh[idx].HouseTimer = g.Gh[idx].HouseTimer - 1
        RETURN
    ENDIF

    DIM spd AS INTEGER = SPD_HOUSE
    g.Gh[idx].MoveAcc = g.Gh[idx].MoveAcc + spd
    IF g.Gh[idx].MoveAcc < 100 THEN RETURN
    g.Gh[idx].MoveAcc = g.Gh[idx].MoveAcc - 100

    ' Step 2: Align horizontally with the door (center X of the house)
    DIM centerX AS INTEGER = T2P(HOUSE_CENTER_X)
    IF g.Gh[idx].X < centerX THEN
        g.Gh[idx].X = g.Gh[idx].X + PX_STEP
        IF g.Gh[idx].X > centerX THEN
            g.Gh[idx].X = centerX
        ENDIF
        RETURN
    ELSEIF g.Gh[idx].X > centerX THEN
        g.Gh[idx].X = g.Gh[idx].X - PX_STEP
        IF g.Gh[idx].X < centerX THEN
            g.Gh[idx].X = centerX
        ENDIF
        RETURN
    ENDIF

    ' Step 3: Float upward through the door
    g.Gh[idx].Y = g.Gh[idx].Y - PX_STEP

    ' Once above the door, the ghost is free! Join the current game mode.
    DIM exitY AS INTEGER = T2P(HOUSE_EXIT_Y)
    IF g.Gh[idx].Y <= exitY THEN
        g.Gh[idx].Y = exitY
        g.Gh[idx].X = T2P(HOUSE_EXIT_X)
        g.Gh[idx].Mode = g.GMode
        g.Gh[idx].Dir = D_LEFT
        g.Gh[idx].MoveAcc = 0
    ENDIF
END SUB

' ChooseDir: The ghost's "brain." At each intersection, the ghost must
' decide which way to turn. The decision depends on the ghost's mode:
'
' FRIGHTENED: Pick a random valid direction (run around aimlessly).
'
' ALL OTHER MODES: Use "target tile" navigation.
'   1. Determine a target tile (different for each ghost and mode).
'   2. Look at all possible directions (except reversing - ghosts can
'      never do a U-turn unless forced by a mode change).
'   3. Pick the direction that leads to the tile CLOSEST to the target.
'   4. If tied, prefer: UP > LEFT > DOWN > RIGHT.
'
' In co-op mode, ghosts target the NEAREST alive player instead of
' always targeting player 0. This makes co-op fairer and more fun!
'
' CHASE MODE TARGETS (this is what gives each ghost its personality!):
'   Blinky (red):   Targets PacMan's exact tile. The straightforward hunter.
'   Pinky (pink):   Targets 4 tiles AHEAD of PacMan. The ambusher.
'   Inky (cyan):    Uses a weird formula involving Blinky's position.
'                   The wildcard - unpredictable!
'   Clyde (orange): Targets PacMan when far away, but runs to his corner
'                   when within 8 tiles. The coward.
'
' SCATTER MODE: Each ghost targets its assigned corner of the maze.
' EATEN MODE: Targets the ghost house door (to go home).
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) ChooseDir(idx AS INTEGER)
    DIM tx AS INTEGER = P2T(g.Gh[idx].X)
    DIM ty AS INTEGER = P2T(g.Gh[idx].Y)
    DIM targX AS INTEGER = 0
    DIM targY AS INTEGER = 0
    DIM d AS INTEGER

    ' --- FRIGHTENED MODE: RANDOM DIRECTION ---
    IF g.Gh[idx].Mode = M_FRIGHT THEN
        DIM rev AS INTEGER = Opposite(g.Gh[idx].Dir)
        DIM tries AS INTEGER = 0
        DIM nd AS INTEGER = g.Gh[idx].Dir
        ' Try random directions until we find a valid one
        DO
            DIM r AS INTEGER = RndInt(4) + 1
            IF r <> rev THEN
                IF g.CanGo(tx, ty, r, FALSE) THEN
                    nd = r
                    tries = 20
                ENDIF
            ENDIF
            tries = tries + 1
        LOOP UNTIL tries >= 20
        ' Use the random direction if valid, otherwise fall back
        IF g.CanGo(tx, ty, nd, FALSE) THEN
            g.Gh[idx].Dir = nd
        ELSEIF g.CanGo(tx, ty, g.Gh[idx].Dir, FALSE) THEN
            ' keep going straight
        ELSE
            FOR d = 1 TO 4
                IF d <> rev THEN
                    IF g.CanGo(tx, ty, d, FALSE) THEN
                        g.Gh[idx].Dir = d
                    ENDIF
                ENDIF
            NEXT
        ENDIF
        RETURN
    ENDIF

    ' --- DETERMINE TARGET TILE based on mode and ghost type ---

    ' Figure out which player to target.
    ' In co-op, target the nearest alive player.
    ' In other modes, target the current player.
    DIM targetPl AS INTEGER = g.CurPl
    IF g.GmMode = GM_COOP THEN
        targetPl = g.NearestPl(g.Gh[idx].X, g.Gh[idx].Y)
    ENDIF

    IF g.Gh[idx].Mode = M_EATEN THEN
        ' Eyes are heading back to the ghost house door
        targX = HOUSE_DOOR_X
        targY = HOUSE_DOOR_Y
    ELSEIF g.Gh[idx].Mode = M_SCATTER THEN
        ' Head to this ghost's assigned corner
        targX = g.Gh[idx].ScatX
        targY = g.Gh[idx].ScatY
    ELSE
        ' CHASE MODE - each ghost has a unique targeting strategy
        DIM ptx AS INTEGER = P2T(g.Pl[targetPl].PX)
        DIM pty AS INTEGER = P2T(g.Pl[targetPl].PY)

        IF g.Gh[idx].GType = 0 THEN
            ' BLINKY: Target PacMan's current tile (simple and aggressive)
            targX = ptx
            targY = pty
        ELSEIF g.Gh[idx].GType = 1 THEN
            ' PINKY: Target 4 tiles ahead of PacMan (tries to cut him off)
            targX = ptx + DirDX(g.Pl[targetPl].PDir) * 4
            targY = pty + DirDY(g.Pl[targetPl].PDir) * 4
        ELSEIF g.Gh[idx].GType = 2 THEN
            ' INKY: Complex targeting using Blinky's position
            ' 1. Find the tile 2 spaces ahead of PacMan
            ' 2. Draw a line from Blinky to that tile
            ' 3. Double the length of that line - that's the target!
            DIM ax AS INTEGER = ptx + DirDX(g.Pl[targetPl].PDir) * 2
            DIM ay AS INTEGER = pty + DirDY(g.Pl[targetPl].PDir) * 2
            DIM bx AS INTEGER = P2T(g.Gh[0].X)
            DIM by AS INTEGER = P2T(g.Gh[0].Y)
            targX = 2 * ax - bx
            targY = 2 * ay - by
        ELSE
            ' CLYDE: Chase PacMan when far, flee to corner when close
            DIM dist AS INTEGER = DistSq(tx, ty, ptx, pty)
            IF dist > 64 THEN
                ' More than 8 tiles away - chase PacMan
                targX = ptx
                targY = pty
            ELSE
                ' Too close! Run away to scatter corner
                targX = g.Gh[idx].ScatX
                targY = g.Gh[idx].ScatY
            ENDIF
        ENDIF
    ENDIF

    ' --- CHOOSE THE BEST DIRECTION ---
    ' Try all 4 directions (except reverse). Pick the one that
    ' gets closest to the target tile. Use squared distance for speed.
    DIM bestDir AS INTEGER = g.Gh[idx].Dir
    DIM bestDist AS INTEGER = 999999
    DIM rev2 AS INTEGER = Opposite(g.Gh[idx].Dir)
    DIM dd AS INTEGER = 0

    ' Check directions in priority order: UP, LEFT, DOWN, RIGHT
    ' (If two directions are equally close, the first one checked wins)
    IF D_UP <> rev2 THEN
        IF g.CanGo(tx, ty, D_UP, FALSE) THEN
            dd = DistSq(tx + DirDX(D_UP), ty + DirDY(D_UP), targX, targY)
            IF dd < bestDist THEN
                bestDist = dd
                bestDir = D_UP
            ENDIF
        ENDIF
    ENDIF
    IF D_LEFT <> rev2 THEN
        IF g.CanGo(tx, ty, D_LEFT, FALSE) THEN
            dd = DistSq(tx + DirDX(D_LEFT), ty + DirDY(D_LEFT), targX, targY)
            IF dd < bestDist THEN
                bestDist = dd
                bestDir = D_LEFT
            ENDIF
        ENDIF
    ENDIF
    IF D_DOWN <> rev2 THEN
        IF g.CanGo(tx, ty, D_DOWN, FALSE) THEN
            dd = DistSq(tx + DirDX(D_DOWN), ty + DirDY(D_DOWN), targX, targY)
            IF dd < bestDist THEN
                bestDist = dd
                bestDir = D_DOWN
            ENDIF
        ENDIF
    ENDIF
    IF D_RIGHT <> rev2 THEN
        IF g.CanGo(tx, ty, D_RIGHT, FALSE) THEN
            dd = DistSq(tx + DirDX(D_RIGHT), ty + DirDY(D_RIGHT), targX, targY)
            IF dd < bestDist THEN
                bestDist = dd
                bestDir = D_RIGHT
            ENDIF
        ENDIF
    ENDIF

    g.Gh[idx].Dir = bestDir
END SUB

' ======================== DRAWING ========================
' Everything below this point is about painting the game on screen.
' The game engine calls Draw() automatically after each Update().
' Draw() should NEVER modify game state - it only reads and renders.

' Draw: The main drawing function. Routes to the appropriate drawing
' method based on game state (intro, playing, game over, etc).
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) Draw(screen AS POINTER TO ebiten.Image)
    screen.Fill(color.RGBA{R: 0, G: 0, B: 0, A: 255})

    IF g.State = S_INTRO THEN
        g.DrawIntro(screen)
        RETURN
    ENDIF

    IF g.State = S_HISCORE THEN
        g.DrawHiScoreEntry(screen)
        RETURN
    ENDIF

    g.DrawMaze(screen)

    ' Draw all alive players. Flash during death animation.
    DIM pi AS INTEGER
    FOR pi = 0 TO g.NumPl - 1
        IF g.Pl[pi].Alive THEN
            DIM shouldDraw AS BOOLEAN = TRUE
            IF g.State = S_DYING THEN
                IF pi = g.AltDying THEN
                    ' Dying player flashes on/off
                    IF g.STimer MOD 10 >= 7 THEN
                        shouldDraw = FALSE
                    ENDIF
                ENDIF
            ENDIF
            IF shouldDraw THEN
                g.DrawPlayer(screen, pi)
            ENDIF
        ENDIF
    NEXT

    ' Hide ghosts during death animation
    IF g.State <> S_DYING THEN
        g.DrawGhosts(screen)
    ENDIF

    g.DrawHUD(screen)
END SUB

' ======================== INTRO / TITLE SCREEN DRAWING ========================
' Shows the game title, a PacMan logo, the menu, and the high score table.

SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) DrawIntro(screen AS POINTER TO ebiten.Image)
    ' --- TITLE ---
    DIM titleX AS INTEGER = SCRW / 2 - 60
    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "PAC-MAN", titleX - 10, 40)
    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "DBasic Edition", titleX - 25, 60)

    ' Draw a decorative PacMan and ghost
    vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, Sng(SCRW / 2 - 50), Sng(110), Sng(20), color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 255, B: 0, A: 255}, FALSE)
    ' Mouth
    vector.DrawFilledRect(screen, Sng(SCRW / 2 - 50), Sng(106), Sng(20), Sng(2), color.RGBA{R: 0, G: 0, B: 0, A: 255}, FALSE)
    vector.DrawFilledRect(screen, Sng(SCRW / 2 - 50), Sng(112), Sng(20), Sng(2), color.RGBA{R: 0, G: 0, B: 0, A: 255}, FALSE)
    ' Decorative ghost
    vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, Sng(SCRW / 2 + 50), Sng(108), Sng(16), color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 0, B: 0, A: 255}, FALSE)
    vector.DrawFilledRect(screen, Sng(SCRW / 2 + 34), Sng(108), Sng(32), Sng(16), color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 0, B: 0, A: 255}, FALSE)
    ' Ghost eyes
    vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, Sng(SCRW / 2 + 44), Sng(105), Sng(4), color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 255, B: 255, A: 255}, FALSE)
    vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, Sng(SCRW / 2 + 56), Sng(105), Sng(4), color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 255, B: 255, A: 255}, FALSE)
    vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, Sng(SCRW / 2 + 43), Sng(105), Sng(2), color.RGBA{R: 33, G: 33, B: 255, A: 255}, FALSE)
    vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, Sng(SCRW / 2 + 55), Sng(105), Sng(2), color.RGBA{R: 33, G: 33, B: 255, A: 255}, FALSE)

    ' --- MENU ---
    DIM menuY AS INTEGER = 170
    DIM menuX AS INTEGER = SCRW / 2 - 55

    ' Menu option labels
    DIM opt0 AS STRING = "  1 PLAYER"
    DIM opt1 AS STRING = "  2P ALTERNATING"
    DIM opt2 AS STRING = "  2P CO-OP"

    ' Add arrow indicator to selected option
    IF g.MenuSel = 0 THEN
        opt0 = "> 1 PLAYER"
    ELSEIF g.MenuSel = 1 THEN
        opt1 = "> 2P ALTERNATING"
    ELSE
        opt2 = "> 2P CO-OP"
    ENDIF

    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, opt0, menuX, menuY)
    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, opt1, menuX, menuY + 20)
    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, opt2, menuX, menuY + 40)

    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "Up/Down to select, Enter to start", SCRW / 2 - 100, menuY + 70)

    ' --- HIGH SCORES TABLE ---
    DIM hsY AS INTEGER = 310
    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "HIGH SCORES", SCRW / 2 - 35, hsY)
    DIM si AS INTEGER
    FOR si = 0 TO LEN(g.HiScores) - 1
        IF si >= MAX_HISCORES THEN
            RETURN
        ENDIF
        DIM rank AS STRING = Str(si + 1) & ". " & g.HiScores[si].Initials & "  " & Str(g.HiScores[si].Pts)
        ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, rank, SCRW / 2 - 50, hsY + 20 + si * 18)
    NEXT

    ' --- CONTROLS HELP ---
    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "1P: WASD or Arrows", SCRW / 2 - 60, 480)
    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "Co-op: P1=WASD  P2=Arrows", SCRW / 2 - 80, 500)
END SUB

' ======================== HIGH SCORE ENTRY DRAWING ========================
' Shows the current score and lets the player enter 3-letter initials.
' Letters scroll with Up/Down, cursor moves with Left/Right.

SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) DrawHiScoreEntry(screen AS POINTER TO ebiten.Image)
    DIM activeP AS INTEGER = g.HiPlIdx
    DIM pLabel AS STRING = "PLAYER " & Str(activeP + 1)

    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "NEW HIGH SCORE!", SCRW / 2 - 50, 80)
    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, pLabel, SCRW / 2 - 30, 110)
    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "SCORE: " & Str(g.Pl[activeP].Score), SCRW / 2 - 40, 140)

    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "ENTER YOUR INITIALS:", SCRW / 2 - 65, 200)

    ' Draw the 3 letter slots
    DIM baseX AS INTEGER = SCRW / 2 - 30
    DIM baseY AS INTEGER = 240
    DIM li AS INTEGER
    FOR li = 0 TO 2
        DIM letter AS STRING = Chr(g.HiName[li] + 65)
        DIM lx AS INTEGER = baseX + li * 25

        ' Draw box around each letter
        IF li = g.HiCursor THEN
            ' Highlighted cursor position - yellow box
            vector.DrawFilledRect(screen, Sng(lx - 3), Sng(baseY - 3), Sng(20), Sng(20), color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 255, B: 0, A: 255}, FALSE)
            ' Black background for the letter
            vector.DrawFilledRect(screen, Sng(lx - 1), Sng(baseY - 1), Sng(16), Sng(16), color.RGBA{R: 0, G: 0, B: 0, A: 255}, FALSE)
        ENDIF

        ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, letter, lx, baseY)
    NEXT

    ' Draw up/down arrows on the cursor position
    DIM cursorX AS INTEGER = baseX + g.HiCursor * 25
    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "^", cursorX + 2, baseY - 20)
    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "v", cursorX + 2, baseY + 20)

    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "Up/Down: change letter", SCRW / 2 - 70, 320)
    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "Left/Right: move cursor", SCRW / 2 - 70, 340)
    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "Enter: confirm", SCRW / 2 - 45, 360)

    ' Show current high score table
    DIM hsY AS INTEGER = 410
    ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "HIGH SCORES", SCRW / 2 - 35, hsY)
    DIM si AS INTEGER
    FOR si = 0 TO LEN(g.HiScores) - 1
        IF si >= MAX_HISCORES THEN
            RETURN
        ENDIF
        DIM rank AS STRING = Str(si + 1) & ". " & g.HiScores[si].Initials & "  " & Str(g.HiScores[si].Pts)
        ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, rank, SCRW / 2 - 50, hsY + 20 + si * 18)
    NEXT
END SUB

' DrawMaze: First stamps the pre-rendered wall image, then draws dots
' and power pellets on top. Power pellets blink by skipping some frames.
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) DrawMaze(screen AS POINTER TO ebiten.Image)
    ' Stamp the cached wall image (super fast - just one image copy)
    screen.DrawImage(g.WallImg, NIL)

    ' Draw dots and power pellets (these change as PacMan eats them)
    DIM x AS INTEGER
    DIM y AS INTEGER
    FOR y = 0 TO MH - 1
        FOR x = 0 TO MW - 1
            DIM cell AS INTEGER = g.Maze[y * MW + x]
            IF cell = C_DOT THEN
                ' Small pink circle for regular dots
                vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, Sng(x * TILE + TILE / 2), Sng(y * TILE + HUD_TOP + TILE / 2), Sng(2), color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 183, B: 174, A: 255}, FALSE)
            ELSEIF cell = C_POWER THEN
                ' Larger blinking pink circle for power pellets
                ' (visible 14 out of every 20 frames = blinking effect)
                IF g.Frame MOD 20 < 14 THEN
                    vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, Sng(x * TILE + TILE / 2), Sng(y * TILE + HUD_TOP + TILE / 2), Sng(5), color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 183, B: 174, A: 255}, FALSE)
                ENDIF
            ENDIF
        NEXT
    NEXT
END SUB

' DrawPlayer: Draws PacMan with a proper pie-shaped wedge mouth that
' opens and closes, just like the real arcade game!
'
' HOW THE MOUTH WORKS:
'   1. Draw a full yellow circle (PacMan's body)
'   2. Draw a black V-shaped wedge on top (the mouth opening)
'   The wedge points in the direction PacMan is facing.
'   The wedge width (mouthW) controls how wide the mouth opens.
'   It cycles: closed -> half open -> full open -> half open -> closed...
'
' The wedge is drawn as a series of thin black lines fanning out from
' PacMan's center toward the facing direction. At distance d from center,
' the mouth is mouthW * d / radius pixels wide. This creates a perfect
' V shape, just like a pizza slice!
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) DrawPlayer(screen AS POINTER TO ebiten.Image, pIdx AS INTEGER)
    DIM cx AS INTEGER = g.Pl[pIdx].PX
    DIM cy AS INTEGER = g.Pl[pIdx].PY + HUD_TOP
    DIM r AS INTEGER = TILE / 2 - 1
    DIM dir AS INTEGER = g.Pl[pIdx].PDir

    ' Compute mouth opening width from animation timer (0-15 cycle).
    ' Phase 0: closed, Phase 1: half, Phase 2: full, Phase 3: half
    DIM phase AS INTEGER = g.Pl[pIdx].MouthT / 4
    DIM mouthW AS INTEGER = 0
    IF phase = 1 THEN
        mouthW = 3
    ELSEIF phase = 2 THEN
        mouthW = 6
    ELSEIF phase = 3 THEN
        mouthW = 3
    ENDIF

    ' When not moving, show closed mouth
    IF dir = D_NONE THEN
        mouthW = 0
    ENDIF

    ' Draw the body circle: P1=yellow, P2=green
    IF g.Pl[pIdx].Clr = 0 THEN
        vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, Sng(cx), Sng(cy), Sng(r), color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 255, B: 0, A: 255}, FALSE)
    ELSE
        vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, Sng(cx), Sng(cy), Sng(r), color.RGBA{R: 0, G: 255, B: 100, A: 255}, FALSE)
    ENDIF

    ' Draw the mouth wedge (V-shaped black cutout)
    IF mouthW > 0 THEN
        DIM d AS INTEGER
        DIM spread AS INTEGER
        IF dir = D_RIGHT THEN
            ' Mouth opens to the right: draw vertical black slices
            FOR d = 1 TO r
                spread = mouthW * d / r
                IF spread > 0 THEN
                    vector.DrawFilledRect(screen, Sng(cx + d), Sng(cy - spread), Sng(1), Sng(spread * 2 + 1), color.RGBA{R: 0, G: 0, B: 0, A: 255}, FALSE)
                ENDIF
            NEXT
        ELSEIF dir = D_LEFT THEN
            ' Mouth opens to the left
            FOR d = 1 TO r
                spread = mouthW * d / r
                IF spread > 0 THEN
                    vector.DrawFilledRect(screen, Sng(cx - d), Sng(cy - spread), Sng(1), Sng(spread * 2 + 1), color.RGBA{R: 0, G: 0, B: 0, A: 255}, FALSE)
                ENDIF
            NEXT
        ELSEIF dir = D_UP THEN
            ' Mouth opens upward: draw horizontal black slices
            FOR d = 1 TO r
                spread = mouthW * d / r
                IF spread > 0 THEN
                    vector.DrawFilledRect(screen, Sng(cx - spread), Sng(cy - d), Sng(spread * 2 + 1), Sng(1), color.RGBA{R: 0, G: 0, B: 0, A: 255}, FALSE)
                ENDIF
            NEXT
        ELSEIF dir = D_DOWN THEN
            ' Mouth opens downward
            FOR d = 1 TO r
                spread = mouthW * d / r
                IF spread > 0 THEN
                    vector.DrawFilledRect(screen, Sng(cx - spread), Sng(cy + d), Sng(spread * 2 + 1), Sng(1), color.RGBA{R: 0, G: 0, B: 0, A: 255}, FALSE)
                ENDIF
            NEXT
        ENDIF
    ENDIF
END SUB

' DrawGhosts: Draws each ghost differently based on its mode:
'   - EATEN: Just floating eyeballs (no body)
'   - ENTERING HOUSE: Same as eaten (eyes moving into the house)
'   - FRIGHTENED: Blue body (flashes white when about to wear off)
'   - NORMAL: Colored body with eyes (Red, Pink, Cyan, or Orange)
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) DrawGhosts(screen AS POINTER TO ebiten.Image)
    DIM i AS INTEGER
    FOR i = 0 TO 3
        DIM gx AS SINGLE = Sng(g.Gh[i].X)
        DIM gy AS SINGLE = Sng(g.Gh[i].Y + HUD_TOP)
        DIM r AS SINGLE = Sng(TILE / 2 - 1)

        IF g.Gh[i].Mode = M_EATEN THEN
            ' Just the eyes - body has been eaten!
            g.DrawEyes(screen, gx, gy, g.Gh[i].Dir)
        ELSEIF g.Gh[i].Mode = M_ENTER THEN
            ' Eyes entering the house
            g.DrawEyes(screen, gx, gy, D_DOWN)
        ELSEIF g.Gh[i].Mode = M_FRIGHT THEN
            ' Frightened ghost: blue body that flashes white near the end
            IF g.Gh[i].FTimer < T_FLASH THEN
                IF g.Gh[i].FTimer MOD 20 < 10 THEN
                    ' Flash WHITE to warn the player fright is ending
                    vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, gx, gy - Sng(2), r, color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 255, B: 255, A: 255}, FALSE)
                    vector.DrawFilledRect(screen, gx - r, gy - Sng(2), r * Sng(2), r, color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 255, B: 255, A: 255}, FALSE)
                ELSE
                    vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, gx, gy - Sng(2), r, color.RGBA{R: 33, G: 33, B: 222, A: 255}, FALSE)
                    vector.DrawFilledRect(screen, gx - r, gy - Sng(2), r * Sng(2), r, color.RGBA{R: 33, G: 33, B: 222, A: 255}, FALSE)
                ENDIF
            ELSE
                ' Solid BLUE body
                vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, gx, gy - Sng(2), r, color.RGBA{R: 33, G: 33, B: 222, A: 255}, FALSE)
                vector.DrawFilledRect(screen, gx - r, gy - Sng(2), r * Sng(2), r, color.RGBA{R: 33, G: 33, B: 222, A: 255}, FALSE)
            ENDIF
        ELSE
            ' Normal ghost: colored body (circle head + rectangle body) + eyes
            DIM clr AS color.RGBA = g.GhostColor(g.Gh[i].GType)
            vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, gx, gy - Sng(2), r, clr, FALSE)
            vector.DrawFilledRect(screen, gx - r, gy - Sng(2), r * Sng(2), r, clr, FALSE)
            g.DrawEyes(screen, gx, gy, g.Gh[i].Dir)
        ENDIF
    NEXT
END SUB

' DrawEyes: Draws two googly eyes on a ghost. The pupils move to point
' in the direction the ghost is traveling. This is especially fun to watch
' when a ghost is eaten and only the eyes remain!
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) DrawEyes(screen AS POINTER TO ebiten.Image, gx AS SINGLE, gy AS SINGLE, dir AS INTEGER)
    ' White part of each eye
    vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, gx - Sng(3), gy - Sng(3), Sng(3), color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 255, B: 255, A: 255}, FALSE)
    vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, gx + Sng(3), gy - Sng(3), Sng(3), color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 255, B: 255, A: 255}, FALSE)

    ' Blue pupils - offset based on direction (they "look" where they're going)
    DIM pdx AS SINGLE = Sng(0)
    DIM pdy AS SINGLE = Sng(0)
    IF dir = D_LEFT THEN
        pdx = Sng(-1)
    ELSEIF dir = D_RIGHT THEN
        pdx = Sng(1)
    ELSEIF dir = D_UP THEN
        pdy = Sng(-1)
    ELSEIF dir = D_DOWN THEN
        pdy = Sng(1)
    ENDIF

    vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, gx - Sng(3) + pdx, gy - Sng(3) + pdy, Sng(1), color.RGBA{R: 33, G: 33, B: 255, A: 255}, FALSE)
    vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, gx + Sng(3) + pdx, gy - Sng(3) + pdy, Sng(1), color.RGBA{R: 33, G: 33, B: 255, A: 255}, FALSE)
END SUB

' GhostColor: Returns the signature color for each ghost type.
'   0 = Blinky -> Red
'   1 = Pinky  -> Pink
'   2 = Inky   -> Cyan (light blue)
'   3 = Clyde  -> Orange
FUNCTION (g AS POINTER TO Game) GhostColor(gtype AS INTEGER) AS color.RGBA
    IF gtype = 0 THEN
        RETURN color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 0, B: 0, A: 255}
    ELSEIF gtype = 1 THEN
        RETURN color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 184, B: 255, A: 255}
    ELSEIF gtype = 2 THEN
        RETURN color.RGBA{R: 0, G: 255, B: 255, A: 255}
    ENDIF
    RETURN color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 184, B: 82, A: 255}
END FUNCTION

' DrawHUD: Draws the "heads-up display" - score, level number, remaining
' lives (shown as small colored circles), and any status messages.
' Adapts to show information for all players based on game mode.
SUB (g AS POINTER TO Game) DrawHUD(screen AS POINTER TO ebiten.Image)
    DIM i AS INTEGER

    IF g.GmMode = GM_SINGLE THEN
        ' Single player: score on left, level on right
        ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "SCORE: " & Str(g.Pl[0].Score), 10, 8)
        ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "LEVEL: " & Str(g.Level), SCRW / 2, 8)

        ' Draw remaining lives as small PacMan icons at the bottom
        FOR i = 0 TO g.Pl[0].Lives - 2
            DIM lx AS SINGLE = Sng(20 + i * 20)
            DIM ly AS SINGLE = Sng(MH * TILE + HUD_TOP + 14)
            vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, lx, ly, Sng(6), color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 255, B: 0, A: 255}, FALSE)
        NEXT

    ELSE
        ' Multiplayer: P1 score on left, P2 score on right, level in center
        ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "P1:" & Str(g.Pl[0].Score), 5, 4)
        IF g.NumPl > 1 THEN
            ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "P2:" & Str(g.Pl[1].Score), SCRW - 90, 4)
        ENDIF
        ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "LV:" & Str(g.Level), SCRW / 2 - 15, 4)

        ' Show whose turn it is in alternating mode
        IF g.GmMode = GM_ALTER THEN
            IF g.State = S_PLAY THEN
                DIM turnLabel AS STRING = "P" & Str(g.CurPl + 1) & " TURN"
                ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, turnLabel, SCRW / 2 - 20, 16)
            ENDIF
        ENDIF

        ' Draw lives for P1 (yellow circles, bottom left)
        FOR i = 0 TO g.Pl[0].Lives - 2
            DIM lx1 AS SINGLE = Sng(20 + i * 16)
            DIM ly1 AS SINGLE = Sng(MH * TILE + HUD_TOP + 14)
            vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, lx1, ly1, Sng(5), color.RGBA{R: 255, G: 255, B: 0, A: 255}, FALSE)
        NEXT
        ' Draw lives for P2 (green circles, bottom right)
        IF g.NumPl > 1 THEN
            DIM p2Lives AS INTEGER = g.Pl[1].Lives - 1
            FOR i = 0 TO p2Lives - 1
                DIM lx2 AS SINGLE = Sng(SCRW - 20 - i * 16)
                DIM ly2 AS SINGLE = Sng(MH * TILE + HUD_TOP + 14)
                vector.DrawFilledCircle(screen, lx2, ly2, Sng(5), color.RGBA{R: 0, G: 255, B: 100, A: 255}, FALSE)
            NEXT
        ENDIF
    ENDIF

    ' Status messages displayed in the center of the maze
    DIM msgX AS INTEGER = SCRW / 2 - 40
    DIM msgY AS INTEGER = 14 * TILE + HUD_TOP

    IF g.State = S_READY THEN
        ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "READY!", msgX, msgY)
    ELSEIF g.State = S_OVER THEN
        ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "GAME OVER", msgX - 10, msgY)
        ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "Press ENTER", msgX - 15, msgY + 20)
    ELSEIF g.State = S_WON THEN
        ebitenutil.DebugPrintAt(screen, "LEVEL CLEAR!", msgX - 15, msgY)
    ENDIF
END SUB

' Layout: Tells the game engine what resolution to use for our game.
' The window can be any size, and the engine will scale our game to fit.
FUNCTION (g AS POINTER TO Game) Layout(ow AS INTEGER, oh AS INTEGER) AS (INTEGER, INTEGER)
    RETURN SCRW, SCRH
END FUNCTION

' ======================== MAIN (Entry Point) ========================
' This is where the program starts! It:
'   1. Locks the game to 60 ticks per second (consistent speed everywhere)
'   2. Creates a new game (starts on the title screen)
'   3. Opens a window (2x scaled so it's not tiny)
'   4. Starts the game loop (Update/Draw run automatically forever)
SUB Main()
    ebiten.SetTPS(60)
    ' Create the audio context ONCE (Ebitengine only allows one).
    ' 44100 Hz is CD-quality sample rate.
    GAudioCtx = audio.NewContext(44100)
    DIM g AS Game = NewGame()
    ebiten.SetWindowSize(SCRW * 2, SCRH * 2)
    ebiten.SetWindowTitle("DBasic PacMan")
    DIM err AS ERROR = ebiten.RunGame(@g)
    IF err <> NIL THEN
        fmt.Println("Error:", err)
    ENDIF
END SUB
